1
00:01:10,989 --> 00:01:12,240
Fifty years ago,

2
00:01:12,657 --> 00:01:15,910
an alien force known
as the Formics attacked Earth.

3
00:01:16,494 --> 00:01:18,162
Tens of millions died.

4
00:01:19,831 --> 00:01:21,499
It was only through the sacrifice

5
00:01:21,583 --> 00:01:22,667
of our greatest commander

6
00:01:23,084 --> 00:01:25,545
that we avoided total annihilation.

7
00:01:39,267 --> 00:01:42,437
We've been preparing for them
to come back ever since.

8
00:01:43,688 --> 00:01:47,191
The International Fleet decided
that the world's smartest children

9
00:01:47,275 --> 00:01:49,110
are the planet's best hope.

10
00:01:49,485 --> 00:01:50,987
Raised on war games,

11
00:01:51,029 --> 00:01:55,283
their decisions are intuitive,
decisive, fearless.

12
00:01:55,950 --> 00:01:57,702
I am one of those recruits.

13
00:01:57,744 --> 00:02:00,079
No, I got him. He's poking his head out.

14
00:02:00,455 --> 00:02:02,040
I've watched through his eyes,

15
00:02:03,166 --> 00:02:04,917
I've listened through his ears,

16
00:02:05,376 --> 00:02:06,961
and I tell you

17
00:02:07,795 --> 00:02:08,880
he's the one.

18
00:02:09,005 --> 00:02:11,174
That's what you said about his brother.

19
00:02:11,758 --> 00:02:14,260
Brother tested out impossible
for other reasons.

20
00:02:14,344 --> 00:02:16,721
Nothing to do with his tactical abilities.

21
00:02:17,555 --> 00:02:19,891
- I gotcha, I gotcha...
- Go around. Go back.

22
00:02:19,932 --> 00:02:21,267
He's gonna crush him.

23
00:02:25,021 --> 00:02:26,189
Come on!

24
00:02:27,273 --> 00:02:28,399
You can't do that!

25
00:02:28,441 --> 00:02:30,151
You've got to use what's around you.

26
00:02:30,234 --> 00:02:31,736
No, no, no. I had you
all the way through the belt!

27
00:02:31,819 --> 00:02:33,237
You miscalculated your trajectory

28
00:02:33,321 --> 00:02:34,947
relative to the incoming asteroid.

29
00:02:35,239 --> 00:02:37,075
Don't lecture me, Wiggin!

30
00:02:37,158 --> 00:02:38,242
You cheated!

31
00:02:39,744 --> 00:02:41,329
It was a good game.

32
00:02:42,413 --> 00:02:43,414
Thanks.

33
00:02:47,210 --> 00:02:48,419
Hey!

34
00:02:53,758 --> 00:02:55,093
Play again.

35
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:57,011
Sorry.

36
00:02:57,345 --> 00:02:59,222
- Tomorrow maybe?
- You see?

37
00:02:59,263 --> 00:03:01,349
He's got a talent for strategy.

38
00:03:01,432 --> 00:03:03,601
His humility could be false.

39
00:03:03,685 --> 00:03:05,853
Part of a strategy to avoid antagonizing

40
00:03:05,937 --> 00:03:07,313
an ego-driven opponent.

41
00:03:07,397 --> 00:03:09,232
Which makes him even smarter.

42
00:03:09,273 --> 00:03:10,316
He may be a genius,

43
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:12,777
but we need someone the others
will follow. A leader.

44
00:03:13,194 --> 00:03:14,862
He can't win on his own.

45
00:03:14,946 --> 00:03:17,573
Well, let's see how he handles rejection.

46
00:03:18,282 --> 00:03:19,992
Andrew Wiggin.

47
00:03:20,076 --> 00:03:21,786
Andrew Ender Wiggin,

48
00:03:21,869 --> 00:03:23,871
please report to the Infirmary.

49
00:03:24,288 --> 00:03:26,332
Ender Wiggin, to the Infirmary.

50
00:03:34,549 --> 00:03:36,634
- Hello, Ender.
- Hello.

51
00:03:36,718 --> 00:03:38,928
That nasty monitor is coming out today.

52
00:03:39,137 --> 00:03:41,013
Please. Lie face down.

53
00:03:42,390 --> 00:03:43,599
Am I off the program?

54
00:03:45,184 --> 00:03:46,477
Did I do something wrong?

55
00:03:46,519 --> 00:03:48,229
That's not really for me to say.

56
00:03:56,529 --> 00:03:57,822
Lie down.

57
00:03:59,115 --> 00:04:01,492
The sooner we get this done,
the sooner you can move on.

58
00:04:14,130 --> 00:04:15,423
Ready?

59
00:04:15,506 --> 00:04:16,966
This won't hurt a bit.

60
00:04:34,525 --> 00:04:36,694
A-ten-hut!

61
00:04:37,361 --> 00:04:38,654
Forward march!

62
00:04:50,374 --> 00:04:52,376
Where do you think you're going, Wiggin?

63
00:04:54,712 --> 00:04:55,713
Washed out, huh?

64
00:04:56,714 --> 00:04:57,882
Come on!

65
00:04:58,883 --> 00:05:00,551
- Get him in there!
- You're expecting...

66
00:05:00,593 --> 00:05:01,761
Come on!

67
00:05:06,265 --> 00:05:07,266
Come on, cheat.

68
00:05:07,767 --> 00:05:09,727
One on one, for real this time.

69
00:05:09,936 --> 00:05:10,937
No game.

70
00:05:11,229 --> 00:05:12,438
He's got no monitor now.

71
00:05:12,522 --> 00:05:13,898
That's right.

72
00:05:13,981 --> 00:05:15,733
There's no one watching you now, Wiggin.

73
00:05:16,984 --> 00:05:18,444
One on one?

74
00:05:18,903 --> 00:05:20,404
Then why are your boys holding me?

75
00:05:23,825 --> 00:05:26,494
- Let's go.
- Come on, man.

76
00:05:37,839 --> 00:05:38,923
Stay down...

77
00:05:39,048 --> 00:05:40,633
I'm gonna kill you, cheat.

78
00:05:40,758 --> 00:05:41,801
Goddamn...

79
00:05:44,929 --> 00:05:46,138
Take it easy, Ender!

80
00:05:52,103 --> 00:05:54,480
You might be thinking of ganging up on me.

81
00:05:55,106 --> 00:05:57,608
But just remember what I do
to people who try to hurt me.

82
00:06:12,790 --> 00:06:14,292
He said I was cheating.

83
00:06:14,375 --> 00:06:16,294
Said that was why I was off the program,

84
00:06:16,377 --> 00:06:18,588
- and I kept on kicking him.
- It doesn't matter.

85
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:20,089
Even after he was down.

86
00:06:20,172 --> 00:06:21,549
He'll never bully you again.

87
00:06:21,632 --> 00:06:23,092
All I could think was,

88
00:06:24,218 --> 00:06:25,511
"What would Peter do?"

89
00:06:28,806 --> 00:06:29,974
I'm just like him, Val.

90
00:06:30,349 --> 00:06:32,810
No. No, you are nothing like him, Ender.

91
00:06:32,935 --> 00:06:34,312
Nothing like who?

92
00:06:34,645 --> 00:06:35,771
I thought you had a game.

93
00:06:36,063 --> 00:06:37,064
Rained out.

94
00:06:37,148 --> 00:06:39,191
- What's he crying about?
- I'm not crying.

95
00:06:39,984 --> 00:06:41,277
My monitor's gone.

96
00:06:41,819 --> 00:06:42,904
Now I'm just like you.

97
00:06:43,279 --> 00:06:45,656
You mean that Mom and Dad spent
all that money on a third,

98
00:06:45,698 --> 00:06:47,074
and now he's off the program too?

99
00:06:47,199 --> 00:06:49,452
Stop it, Peter. He made it
farther than either of us.

100
00:06:49,577 --> 00:06:50,578
Hey, dropout.

101
00:06:51,412 --> 00:06:53,247
Remember how to play
Formics and Astronauts?

102
00:06:53,372 --> 00:06:54,916
That's it! Where's Mom?

103
00:06:55,583 --> 00:06:56,834
No, don't.

104
00:06:58,210 --> 00:06:59,587
- I'll play.
- Put the mask on.

105
00:07:00,421 --> 00:07:01,839
You can be the bug.

106
00:07:03,549 --> 00:07:05,009
Peter! You're insane!

107
00:07:05,051 --> 00:07:07,386
- Stay out of this, Valentine!
- No! Stop it!

108
00:07:07,470 --> 00:07:09,138
All right, bug, you started
it, you attack first.

109
00:07:09,347 --> 00:07:10,348
Peter! Let me in!

110
00:07:10,431 --> 00:07:11,432
Come on!

111
00:07:14,477 --> 00:07:15,853
Come on, fight back!

112
00:07:16,187 --> 00:07:17,271
At last we got one of you alive!

113
00:07:17,355 --> 00:07:19,023
Peter! Stop it!

114
00:07:19,982 --> 00:07:22,193
You know, I could kill you, just like this.

115
00:07:23,945 --> 00:07:25,821
Peter... Please...

116
00:07:26,697 --> 00:07:27,782
I should have been chosen.

117
00:07:38,542 --> 00:07:40,586
Deep space intel shows us

118
00:07:40,795 --> 00:07:43,297
that the number of enemy ships
already deployed

119
00:07:43,381 --> 00:07:46,968
is 10 times those we faced
during the first invasion.

120
00:07:47,051 --> 00:07:49,720
The Formics are rebuilding
and strengthening their fleet.

121
00:07:49,887 --> 00:07:52,223
We must conquer or die.

122
00:07:52,348 --> 00:07:53,891
Turn it off, please, John.

123
00:07:53,933 --> 00:07:55,893
Why? You'd rather not know
what's going on in the world?

124
00:07:56,102 --> 00:07:57,395
We must never again bear witness

125
00:07:57,436 --> 00:08:00,856
to the slaughter of tens of
millions of innocent people,

126
00:08:00,898 --> 00:08:02,775
as we did during the Formic invasion.

127
00:08:02,900 --> 00:08:04,902
I'd rather you talk to your son.

128
00:08:04,944 --> 00:08:06,904
Our survival demands total commitment

129
00:08:06,946 --> 00:08:08,739
to the destruction of the enemy.

130
00:08:09,740 --> 00:08:11,200
If you want, I'll go away,

131
00:08:11,409 --> 00:08:13,369
so you don't have to be embarrassed.

132
00:08:13,411 --> 00:08:15,746
Ender, no one is embarrassed.

133
00:08:16,455 --> 00:08:19,375
I'm a third. I should never have been born.

134
00:08:19,709 --> 00:08:22,753
No. We wanted you, Ender.
We just needed permission.

135
00:08:26,924 --> 00:08:29,301
John, please say something.

136
00:08:32,096 --> 00:08:34,140
It's a tough program, Ender.

137
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:37,935
When they brought me to this country,

138
00:08:37,977 --> 00:08:40,604
there was less competition.
And still, I didn't make it.

139
00:08:41,897 --> 00:08:43,607
You have nothing to be ashamed of.

140
00:08:45,276 --> 00:08:46,485
Nothing.

141
00:08:48,404 --> 00:08:49,780
Sensor alert.

142
00:08:49,822 --> 00:08:52,283
Front door. Please state your name.

143
00:08:52,533 --> 00:08:53,576
Colonel Hyrum Graff,

144
00:08:53,617 --> 00:08:55,453
Director of Training, International Fleet.

145
00:08:55,494 --> 00:08:57,747
This is my colleague, Major Anderson.

146
00:08:58,164 --> 00:08:59,290
May we?

147
00:08:59,832 --> 00:09:01,250
Why'd you keep kicking him?

148
00:09:01,292 --> 00:09:02,752
You'd already won the fight.

149
00:09:02,793 --> 00:09:04,628
- Did you enjoy it?
- No.

150
00:09:05,129 --> 00:09:07,506
Then why? Speak up, son.

151
00:09:10,634 --> 00:09:12,636
Knocking him down was the first fight.

152
00:09:14,805 --> 00:09:16,640
I wanted to win all the next ones too.

153
00:09:18,309 --> 00:09:19,769
So they'd leave me alone.

154
00:09:19,852 --> 00:09:21,604
Ender, you should have asked
a grownup for help.

155
00:09:21,937 --> 00:09:23,939
Nonsense. He can fight his own battles.

156
00:09:24,190 --> 00:09:25,649
Colonel, he was obviously being bullied

157
00:09:25,691 --> 00:09:28,152
- and he defended himself.
- Son...

158
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:31,697
I'd like to offer you a
place in our program.

159
00:09:39,830 --> 00:09:41,540
But you took away my monitor.

160
00:09:41,707 --> 00:09:43,292
The final step in our evaluation

161
00:09:43,334 --> 00:09:45,836
is always to see what happens
when the monitor's removed.

162
00:09:45,878 --> 00:09:47,379
And he passed?

163
00:09:47,463 --> 00:09:49,173
He put a child in the hospital.

164
00:09:49,256 --> 00:09:50,257
It's not what he did.

165
00:09:50,549 --> 00:09:53,177
It's why he did it. It was tactical.

166
00:09:53,385 --> 00:09:56,347
A strategy to stop future attacks.

167
00:09:56,514 --> 00:09:58,849
Ender, you don't have to do this.

168
00:09:59,225 --> 00:10:02,061
Ender and I should have
a private conversation.

169
00:10:02,144 --> 00:10:04,522
- Absolutely not!
- With all respect, sir,

170
00:10:04,605 --> 00:10:06,690
you really can't stop me.

171
00:10:10,528 --> 00:10:12,029
The Formics might have wiped us out

172
00:10:12,113 --> 00:10:13,614
the last time, you know.

173
00:10:15,241 --> 00:10:18,369
A brilliant commander is
the only thing that saved us.

174
00:10:19,995 --> 00:10:21,539
Mazer Rackham.

175
00:10:21,914 --> 00:10:23,415
Mazer Rackham.

176
00:10:23,707 --> 00:10:26,502
We need minds like yours, Ender.

177
00:10:26,669 --> 00:10:30,381
Young people integrate complex
data more easily than adults.

178
00:10:33,050 --> 00:10:34,844
Will the monitor be reinstalled?

179
00:10:35,386 --> 00:10:36,595
No.

180
00:10:37,054 --> 00:10:38,597
You're graduating.

181
00:10:39,223 --> 00:10:40,891
To Battle School.

182
00:10:42,643 --> 00:10:44,687
Privacy rights restored.

183
00:10:46,230 --> 00:10:49,441
If there is a chance that, because of you,

184
00:10:49,733 --> 00:10:52,611
the Formics might leave us alone forever,

185
00:10:54,864 --> 00:10:57,116
then I have to ask you to come with me.

186
00:11:04,498 --> 00:11:06,917
It's what I was born for, right?

187
00:11:10,588 --> 00:11:12,006
Valentine was too compassionate

188
00:11:12,089 --> 00:11:13,757
for Battle School.

189
00:11:20,347 --> 00:11:21,932
My brother Peter washed out

190
00:11:22,016 --> 00:11:24,310
because he was too quick to violence.

191
00:11:25,311 --> 00:11:27,146
Colonel Graff said I need to find a balance

192
00:11:27,229 --> 00:11:29,982
between those emotions
if I were to succeed.

193
00:11:37,072 --> 00:11:38,365
Join the others.

194
00:11:39,783 --> 00:11:40,910
Go on.

195
00:11:57,384 --> 00:11:59,845
- You're late.
- Out of my control.

196
00:12:00,471 --> 00:12:01,639
I'm Ender.

197
00:12:02,890 --> 00:12:03,891
Ender?

198
00:12:04,475 --> 00:12:06,352
What kind of name is that?

199
00:12:07,144 --> 00:12:08,270
What's your name?

200
00:12:10,314 --> 00:12:11,482
Name's Bean.

201
00:12:11,899 --> 00:12:13,067
Bean?

202
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:15,527
Grew up on the streets. Not worth a bean.

203
00:12:26,330 --> 00:12:28,749
T-minus five seconds and counting.

204
00:12:29,875 --> 00:12:33,879
Four, three, two, one...

205
00:12:58,529 --> 00:12:59,947
Wow...

206
00:13:00,281 --> 00:13:01,699
Oh, my gosh!

207
00:13:07,454 --> 00:13:08,539
I'm gonna be...

208
00:13:08,622 --> 00:13:10,291
A bag! Give him the bag!

209
00:13:20,092 --> 00:13:22,052
Are you serious, man?

210
00:13:22,469 --> 00:13:23,637
Close the bag!

211
00:13:27,474 --> 00:13:28,475
You all right?

212
00:13:32,688 --> 00:13:34,481
What are you doin', Wiggin?

213
00:13:34,565 --> 00:13:35,733
Nothing, sir.

214
00:13:35,816 --> 00:13:37,318
Something funny?

215
00:13:37,901 --> 00:13:39,570
I asked you a question, Launchie!

216
00:13:41,322 --> 00:13:43,198
Sir, the way you're floating.

217
00:13:43,615 --> 00:13:45,826
Horizontal. I thought that was funny.

218
00:13:46,493 --> 00:13:47,578
Really? Why?

219
00:13:48,329 --> 00:13:51,415
Because in zero gravity,
there is no right side up.

220
00:13:51,457 --> 00:13:53,667
You may think you're vertical
and we may be horizontal.

221
00:13:55,419 --> 00:13:56,545
Is that funny?

222
00:13:56,587 --> 00:13:57,713
- Sir, no, sir!
- Sir, no, sir!

223
00:13:58,797 --> 00:14:00,090
Yes, it is.

224
00:14:00,841 --> 00:14:02,968
Alai, do you know what he's talkin' about?

225
00:14:03,427 --> 00:14:05,179
- Yes, sir.
- No, you don't.

226
00:14:06,347 --> 00:14:08,349
There's only one kid on this launch

227
00:14:08,432 --> 00:14:10,517
with any brains at all so far.

228
00:14:11,268 --> 00:14:13,645
And that's Ender Wiggin.

229
00:14:51,517 --> 00:14:52,810
All new arrivals

230
00:14:52,893 --> 00:14:55,145
follow the yellow lights
to your accommodations.

231
00:14:55,229 --> 00:14:56,980
The yellow lights.

232
00:15:03,487 --> 00:15:04,696
All new arrivals

233
00:15:04,780 --> 00:15:06,824
follow the yellow lights
to your accommodations.

234
00:15:06,990 --> 00:15:08,492
The yellow lights.

235
00:15:09,493 --> 00:15:11,203
Sir, you made them hate me.

236
00:15:11,286 --> 00:15:12,704
I told them you were the best.

237
00:15:13,038 --> 00:15:14,581
We need a Julius Caesar,

238
00:15:14,665 --> 00:15:16,834
- a Napoleon.
- We hope that will be you.

239
00:15:16,917 --> 00:15:19,503
Caesar was assassinated
by the people he trusted.

240
00:15:19,586 --> 00:15:21,880
And Napoleon lost in the end.

241
00:15:22,005 --> 00:15:24,466
Not before he conquered the known world.

242
00:15:26,093 --> 00:15:28,178
- Dismissed.
- Yes, sir.

243
00:15:32,683 --> 00:15:35,436
He has a complicated response to authority.

244
00:15:35,519 --> 00:15:37,729
He wants to please
the overbearing father figure,

245
00:15:37,813 --> 00:15:40,232
but resents a lack of
reciprocated affection.

246
00:15:40,524 --> 00:15:42,526
His isolation can never be broken.

247
00:15:43,068 --> 00:15:45,779
He must never believe anyone will help him.

248
00:15:47,448 --> 00:15:50,200
Look! It's the smartass.

249
00:15:56,582 --> 00:15:57,583
Thanks.

250
00:15:58,041 --> 00:16:00,252
Thought I'd have to ask to be by the door.

251
00:16:07,926 --> 00:16:09,261
Speak your name.

252
00:16:09,470 --> 00:16:10,888
Ender Wiggin.

253
00:16:17,311 --> 00:16:18,645
Don't freeze your balls, kid.

254
00:16:18,729 --> 00:16:19,938
Attention on deck!

255
00:16:22,566 --> 00:16:23,567
At ease.

256
00:16:24,610 --> 00:16:26,862
Listen up, Launchies!

257
00:16:26,904 --> 00:16:30,491
My name is Sergeant James Dap.

258
00:16:30,741 --> 00:16:32,534
Ask me a legitimate question

259
00:16:32,576 --> 00:16:35,662
and I will give you a direct answer.

260
00:16:35,746 --> 00:16:38,373
But if you are looking
for a shoulder to cry on,

261
00:16:38,415 --> 00:16:39,791
use a pillow!

262
00:16:41,084 --> 00:16:42,920
Do I look like I'm joking, snots?

263
00:16:43,170 --> 00:16:44,796
- Sir, no, sir!
- Sir, no, sir!

264
00:16:44,922 --> 00:16:46,048
Good.

265
00:16:46,256 --> 00:16:48,383
You are to work as a team.

266
00:16:48,425 --> 00:16:50,969
You will all make this bunkroom your home.

267
00:16:51,053 --> 00:16:53,013
You will keep your home clean!

268
00:16:53,096 --> 00:16:55,557
There are separate showers for both sexes.

269
00:16:55,599 --> 00:16:59,102
If you're found in an area not
designated to your gender,

270
00:16:59,144 --> 00:17:01,688
I will personally neuter you!

271
00:17:01,772 --> 00:17:03,273
Am I clear?

272
00:17:03,398 --> 00:17:04,816
- Sir, yes, sir!
- Sir, yes, sir!

273
00:17:09,780 --> 00:17:12,157
Class is in five! Follow the yellow lights!

274
00:17:12,241 --> 00:17:13,867
Yellow, like your cowardly selves!

275
00:17:14,117 --> 00:17:15,452
- Sir, yes, sir!
- Sir, yes, sir!

276
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:19,039
Welcome to Battle School.

277
00:17:19,122 --> 00:17:22,042
A great responsibility
rests upon each of you.

278
00:17:22,292 --> 00:17:25,295
When the enemy first invaded,
we were not ready.

279
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:28,215
Millions of innocent lives were lost.

280
00:17:28,632 --> 00:17:30,842
That must never be allowed
to happen again.

281
00:17:31,134 --> 00:17:33,971
We threw everything we had at the invaders.

282
00:17:34,221 --> 00:17:36,723
And in the midst of that decisive battle,

283
00:17:38,141 --> 00:17:40,310
a legendary hero emerged.

284
00:17:59,830 --> 00:18:01,081
Eject! Eject!

285
00:18:03,250 --> 00:18:06,169
Break away now! Hammer 3!

286
00:18:06,712 --> 00:18:08,422
Hammer 2, break left!

287
00:18:08,839 --> 00:18:10,215
Bend at left, 7 o'clock.

288
00:18:10,424 --> 00:18:12,676
Hammer 2 is hit! Hammer 2 critical!

289
00:18:13,927 --> 00:18:15,512
Hammer 1 has been hit!

290
00:18:35,907 --> 00:18:38,368
We will never forget what the enemy did.

291
00:18:38,869 --> 00:18:40,245
But we defeated them.

292
00:18:41,204 --> 00:18:43,373
And we will do so again.

293
00:18:44,791 --> 00:18:46,543
Let the courage of Mazer Rackham

294
00:18:47,377 --> 00:18:49,087
be your inspiration.

295
00:18:51,089 --> 00:18:53,508
Wakey, wakey, rise and shine!

296
00:18:53,717 --> 00:18:55,052
Put on your Battle Room suits!

297
00:18:55,260 --> 00:18:58,722
That's the padded one with
the helmet and the weapon!

298
00:18:58,764 --> 00:19:02,184
Do not attempt to fire the weapon!
Holster it!

299
00:19:02,434 --> 00:19:04,227
Let's move it, Launchies!

300
00:19:04,394 --> 00:19:05,979
You've got 10 minutes!

301
00:19:16,615 --> 00:19:17,949
At ease.

302
00:19:18,867 --> 00:19:20,243
This is the Battle Room.

303
00:19:20,327 --> 00:19:22,204
In here, the floor has been designed

304
00:19:22,245 --> 00:19:24,873
to create an Earth-like gravitational pull.

305
00:19:25,123 --> 00:19:26,875
Step through that gate

306
00:19:26,917 --> 00:19:30,128
and you're in a zero-G environment.

307
00:19:36,593 --> 00:19:37,594
Wiggin.

308
00:19:39,221 --> 00:19:40,806
Get up here.

309
00:20:08,291 --> 00:20:10,168
What do I do now, sir?

310
00:20:10,419 --> 00:20:11,420
Go on in.

311
00:20:31,356 --> 00:20:33,483
All right. Now, push off.

312
00:21:17,027 --> 00:21:19,029
Pull yourself.

313
00:21:26,536 --> 00:21:28,663
Grab my hand. No, no! Stop! Stop!

314
00:21:29,748 --> 00:21:30,832
Nicely done!

315
00:21:31,917 --> 00:21:33,418
These guys are still trying to stay up,

316
00:21:33,502 --> 00:21:35,086
the way they came in.

317
00:21:35,170 --> 00:21:36,588
Like you said in the shuttle,

318
00:21:36,671 --> 00:21:38,381
there is no up or down in space.

319
00:21:38,465 --> 00:21:41,009
But we'll need some way
to orientate in here.

320
00:21:41,051 --> 00:21:42,886
Maybe the enemy's gate is "down."

321
00:21:43,762 --> 00:21:44,971
I like it.

322
00:21:45,055 --> 00:21:47,265
Like they're a bug to be
crushed under our feet.

323
00:21:47,390 --> 00:21:48,600
Exactly.

324
00:21:54,439 --> 00:21:55,899
What do you think this does?

325
00:21:55,982 --> 00:21:57,442
Let's find out.

326
00:22:07,911 --> 00:22:09,329
Well, that's harmless.

327
00:22:09,830 --> 00:22:12,374
What do you think it does
when it hits the suit?

328
00:22:12,415 --> 00:22:13,792
Good question.

329
00:22:21,716 --> 00:22:22,717
Shoot me in the leg.

330
00:22:22,759 --> 00:22:24,344
We shoot each other. Same time.

331
00:22:27,931 --> 00:22:28,932
You ready?

332
00:22:30,100 --> 00:22:31,309
In three...

333
00:22:31,476 --> 00:22:33,562
- Two, one...
- Two, one...

334
00:22:36,690 --> 00:22:38,024
My leg's frozen!

335
00:22:38,775 --> 00:22:40,026
Mine too!

336
00:22:40,735 --> 00:22:41,945
I can't bend my knee.

337
00:22:45,740 --> 00:22:46,825
Shoot me in the chest.

338
00:22:47,784 --> 00:22:48,994
Come on! I'm getting away!

339
00:22:55,959 --> 00:22:57,335
This is amazing!

340
00:22:57,961 --> 00:22:59,379
I can't move at all now.

341
00:22:59,504 --> 00:23:00,755
You're out of your mind.

342
00:23:02,132 --> 00:23:03,300
That's enough.

343
00:23:19,441 --> 00:23:22,485
You're flappin' around
like a bunch of drunken ducks!

344
00:23:22,569 --> 00:23:23,695
If you expect to compete

345
00:23:23,778 --> 00:23:25,155
with the other teams at this school,

346
00:23:25,238 --> 00:23:26,531
you've got a lot to learn.

347
00:23:26,615 --> 00:23:28,450
Sergeant, explain the game.

348
00:23:28,867 --> 00:23:30,201
Yes, sir.

349
00:23:31,995 --> 00:23:35,832
You will train to compete
as a team against other teams.

350
00:23:35,916 --> 00:23:38,293
You get one point for a hit to a limb,

351
00:23:38,335 --> 00:23:39,669
six for a torso hit,

352
00:23:39,753 --> 00:23:41,504
which will immobilize you completely.

353
00:23:41,546 --> 00:23:44,507
But, if either side gets one cadet

354
00:23:44,549 --> 00:23:47,385
through their enemy's gate unharmed,

355
00:23:47,469 --> 00:23:49,095
that army will win,

356
00:23:49,554 --> 00:23:51,932
regardless of points already scored.

357
00:23:52,015 --> 00:23:53,016
Am I clear?

358
00:23:53,391 --> 00:23:54,851
- Sir, yes, sir!
- Sir, yes, sir!

359
00:23:55,101 --> 00:23:58,188
"Dear Valentine... So
this is Battle School.

360
00:23:58,229 --> 00:24:00,523
"Every day, hours of training.

361
00:24:00,607 --> 00:24:03,193
"And far more homework
than we ever had on Earth.

362
00:24:03,693 --> 00:24:05,403
"We train in hand-to-hand combat.

363
00:24:06,529 --> 00:24:09,532
”It keeps us in shape. And aggressive."

364
00:24:09,616 --> 00:24:10,742
And up!

365
00:24:10,867 --> 00:24:13,119
And one!

366
00:24:13,203 --> 00:24:14,412
Two!

367
00:24:14,537 --> 00:24:15,538
Three!

368
00:24:15,580 --> 00:24:17,874
"I feel Peter in me whenever I fight."

369
00:24:18,416 --> 00:24:21,044
- Wiggin!
- "I wish I didn't.

370
00:24:21,086 --> 00:24:23,421
"We've been studying Formic flight patterns
for three months now,

371
00:24:23,505 --> 00:24:25,215
"but they seem entirely random.

372
00:24:25,298 --> 00:24:27,926
"The truth is we really don't
understand our enemy.

373
00:24:28,009 --> 00:24:30,053
"And no one ever adequately explains

374
00:24:30,136 --> 00:24:32,973
"how Mazer Rackham actually
defeated the entire fleet.

375
00:24:36,101 --> 00:24:37,978
"The Colonel said he expects me to lead.

376
00:24:38,353 --> 00:24:41,064
"But how? What makes a good leader?

377
00:24:41,106 --> 00:24:42,899
"Everyone here is very different.

378
00:24:43,400 --> 00:24:45,735
"So many, many things to learn.

379
00:24:45,777 --> 00:24:47,821
"Always very little sleep.

380
00:24:48,738 --> 00:24:51,074
"Please write back. I
haven't heard from you.

381
00:24:51,825 --> 00:24:54,536
"How are you? ls Peter behaving?

382
00:24:54,619 --> 00:24:56,788
"Are you getting my e-mails? I miss you..."

383
00:24:56,913 --> 00:24:58,248
Attention on deck!

384
00:25:05,672 --> 00:25:07,924
Evening, Launchies. At ease.

385
00:25:09,342 --> 00:25:12,262
I'm pleased to see that most
of you are performing well.

386
00:25:12,345 --> 00:25:15,598
As you know, competition for
Command School is tough.

387
00:25:15,682 --> 00:25:18,601
Some in the higher ranks have
failed to meet our standards

388
00:25:18,685 --> 00:25:20,228
and are being sent home.

389
00:25:20,937 --> 00:25:25,150
So, I may have the opportunity
to promote some of you.

390
00:25:25,233 --> 00:25:26,234
Look to your left.

391
00:25:28,945 --> 00:25:30,030
Look to your right.

392
00:25:31,781 --> 00:25:34,617
These are not your friends.

393
00:25:34,868 --> 00:25:36,828
They are competition.

394
00:25:38,329 --> 00:25:39,622
Keep up the hard work.

395
00:25:39,789 --> 00:25:41,041
Attention!

396
00:25:41,541 --> 00:25:42,792
Sir?

397
00:25:43,501 --> 00:25:45,086
Is our e-mail being blocked?

398
00:25:46,671 --> 00:25:48,882
It's just that none of us have received
any replies from home.

399
00:25:49,632 --> 00:25:52,844
All communication is being
temporarily held back.

400
00:25:52,927 --> 00:25:53,970
Why, sir?

401
00:25:54,012 --> 00:25:55,430
Launchie, it is not your place...

402
00:25:56,639 --> 00:25:59,017
Your families will not understand

403
00:25:59,100 --> 00:26:00,310
what we're doing here.

404
00:26:00,393 --> 00:26:03,980
And none of you need
the distraction of their replies.

405
00:26:04,731 --> 00:26:06,691
I thought our privacy rights
had been restored, sir.

406
00:26:07,650 --> 00:26:09,819
You have the right

407
00:26:09,861 --> 00:26:13,323
to privately think
whatever you wish, Wiggin.

408
00:26:15,158 --> 00:26:16,367
But there's too much at stake

409
00:26:16,451 --> 00:26:18,995
to allow your unfiltered thoughts

410
00:26:19,037 --> 00:26:21,122
to leave this facility.

411
00:26:22,874 --> 00:26:23,875
Yes, sir.

412
00:26:33,510 --> 00:26:34,511
Keep it up, snot,

413
00:26:34,594 --> 00:26:36,096
and you will never make it
to Command School.

414
00:26:36,387 --> 00:26:37,764
I thought it was a legitimate question.

415
00:26:37,847 --> 00:26:38,848
What?

416
00:26:38,890 --> 00:26:40,350
You said if we had a legitimate question...

417
00:26:40,433 --> 00:26:42,519
Drop and give me 20!

418
00:26:52,695 --> 00:26:54,364
You think you're the smartest
kid in this school?

419
00:26:54,739 --> 00:26:55,740
No, sir.

420
00:26:55,907 --> 00:26:59,035
You will never be a commander!
I will never salute you!

421
00:26:59,369 --> 00:27:00,370
Yes, you will, Sergeant.

422
00:27:00,954 --> 00:27:02,413
Give me 20 more!

423
00:27:13,424 --> 00:27:14,425
Get up!

424
00:27:17,554 --> 00:27:20,473
You do not speak unless spoken to!

425
00:27:20,723 --> 00:27:22,350
Am I clear?

426
00:27:22,392 --> 00:27:24,435
- Sir, yes, sir!
- Sir, yes, sir!

427
00:27:25,395 --> 00:27:27,063
Even if I have a legitimate question?

428
00:27:27,105 --> 00:27:28,731
Shut it, Wiggin!

429
00:27:35,947 --> 00:27:37,490
Now go to sleep!

430
00:27:38,199 --> 00:27:39,576
All of you!

431
00:27:52,422 --> 00:27:53,590
You heard him.

432
00:27:54,966 --> 00:27:55,967
Get some sleep.

433
00:28:08,104 --> 00:28:09,272
We have only three passing scores

434
00:28:09,355 --> 00:28:11,274
on the deep space navigation test.

435
00:28:11,691 --> 00:28:13,902
Alai, Bean and Ender.

436
00:28:13,943 --> 00:28:15,987
- What happened here?
- They probably cheated.

437
00:28:16,070 --> 00:28:17,155
Your mother cheated.

438
00:28:17,238 --> 00:28:18,489
That's why you look like a plumber.

439
00:28:18,573 --> 00:28:19,616
Zip it!

440
00:28:19,657 --> 00:28:20,909
You think this is a game?

441
00:28:21,951 --> 00:28:22,952
No, ma'am.

442
00:28:24,287 --> 00:28:26,623
- We are preparing for war.
- Yes, ma'am.

443
00:28:27,999 --> 00:28:29,584
Now, the problem was simple.

444
00:28:29,626 --> 00:28:31,461
How do you slingshot your forces

445
00:28:32,629 --> 00:28:35,340
into an attack position on
the blind side of this moon

446
00:28:35,423 --> 00:28:37,300
using the gravitational pull
from this planet?

447
00:28:37,383 --> 00:28:39,260
This is basic rocket science, people.

448
00:28:39,594 --> 00:28:42,055
Ender, get down here and explain.

449
00:28:43,723 --> 00:28:45,099
Ma'am, I think Bean or Alai

450
00:28:45,141 --> 00:28:46,726
have a better handle on this than I do.

451
00:28:47,644 --> 00:28:50,146
All right. Alai, come and explain.

452
00:28:54,025 --> 00:28:56,027
Ma'am, we need to approach the planet

453
00:28:56,110 --> 00:28:57,111
in the direction it's moving.

454
00:28:58,446 --> 00:29:00,281
That way, we benefit
from its energy of motion.

455
00:29:01,908 --> 00:29:02,992
Is something funny?

456
00:29:06,037 --> 00:29:07,038
Go on, Alai.

457
00:29:08,248 --> 00:29:10,875
Of course, there's
a moon we have to pass here

458
00:29:10,959 --> 00:29:12,418
and that complicates things.

459
00:29:12,710 --> 00:29:14,754
Because the moon's moving in
the opposite direction to us,

460
00:29:14,837 --> 00:29:16,839
we get a gravitational braking.

461
00:29:19,259 --> 00:29:20,260
Who sent this?

462
00:29:21,386 --> 00:29:22,679
Who sent what, Bernard?

463
00:29:24,514 --> 00:29:25,765
Nothing, ma'am.

464
00:29:29,769 --> 00:29:32,355
If you can't take it, Bernard,
don't dish it out.

465
00:29:32,397 --> 00:29:33,606
Yes, ma'am.

466
00:30:27,076 --> 00:30:29,329
Welcome to Games and Recreation.

467
00:30:31,456 --> 00:30:33,708
Cerebral control enabled.

468
00:31:03,404 --> 00:31:06,199
One is poison. One is not.

469
00:31:06,699 --> 00:31:08,785
Choose right and you'll go to Fairyland.

470
00:31:09,494 --> 00:31:10,787
He's found the Mind Game.

471
00:31:12,205 --> 00:31:13,915
Decide or I'll bite your head off.

472
00:31:28,888 --> 00:31:30,473
Bad luck.

473
00:31:31,057 --> 00:31:32,934
Who authorized his access to this?

474
00:31:32,975 --> 00:31:34,769
- I did.
- Try again, little mouse.

475
00:31:34,852 --> 00:31:35,853
To what end?

476
00:31:35,937 --> 00:31:37,855
Not every battle can be won, Hyrum.

477
00:31:37,939 --> 00:31:39,982
The way he plays a game
reveals his state of mind.

478
00:31:40,024 --> 00:31:41,901
If you won't let me assess him one on one,

479
00:31:41,984 --> 00:31:43,736
I need some other way
to know what he's feeling.

480
00:31:43,820 --> 00:31:45,321
I don't care how he's feeling.

481
00:31:46,239 --> 00:31:48,366
I want him to toughen up
and learn how to lead.

482
00:31:48,449 --> 00:31:49,867
Well, before we make him a leader,

483
00:31:49,951 --> 00:31:52,203
let's see how he deals with frustration.

484
00:32:03,881 --> 00:32:05,800
Come on!

485
00:32:05,842 --> 00:32:06,968
Oh, dear.

486
00:32:07,552 --> 00:32:08,678
What you doin'?

487
00:32:09,470 --> 00:32:11,055
Playing a stupid game.

488
00:32:11,180 --> 00:32:13,349
No matter what I choose, I die.
It's rigged.

489
00:32:13,433 --> 00:32:14,559
You're back.

490
00:32:15,017 --> 00:32:16,018
One more time.

491
00:32:16,102 --> 00:32:17,186
Can I watch?

492
00:32:17,270 --> 00:32:18,271
Sure.

493
00:32:20,189 --> 00:32:22,692
One is poison. One is not.

494
00:32:23,234 --> 00:32:25,236
Choose right and you'll go to Fairyland.

495
00:32:25,319 --> 00:32:27,238
- Which you gonna choose?
- Neither.

496
00:32:27,989 --> 00:32:30,032
Come on, little mouse, come on.

497
00:32:49,177 --> 00:32:50,386
You killed him.

498
00:32:50,887 --> 00:32:52,054
Why?

499
00:32:53,681 --> 00:32:54,932
That's what they want from us.

500
00:32:56,058 --> 00:32:59,103
Follow the rules, you lose.
Choose violence, you win.

501
00:32:59,645 --> 00:33:01,898
I've never seen anyone do that.

502
00:33:02,273 --> 00:33:03,524
Perfect.

503
00:33:04,775 --> 00:33:06,068
He's perfect.

504
00:33:08,237 --> 00:33:09,238
Ender Wiggin,

505
00:33:09,322 --> 00:33:10,448
you are assigned to Salamander Army,

506
00:33:10,531 --> 00:33:11,657
Commander Bonzo Madrid,

507
00:33:11,741 --> 00:33:14,410
effective immediately.
Orders of Colonel Graff.

508
00:33:14,744 --> 00:33:17,705
Follow the green lights.
Take nothing with you. Go now.

509
00:33:19,957 --> 00:33:21,250
What are they doing?

510
00:33:21,834 --> 00:33:23,586
They're promoting you.

511
00:33:33,846 --> 00:33:34,847
Ender...

512
00:33:36,432 --> 00:33:37,433
Yeah?

513
00:33:43,189 --> 00:33:44,565
Peace to you.

514
00:33:53,324 --> 00:33:54,951
- Throw!
- Come on!

515
00:33:54,992 --> 00:33:56,035
- Ball...
- Strike two!

516
00:33:56,244 --> 00:33:57,912
- Give me the ball.
- It hit the wall!

517
00:33:58,162 --> 00:34:00,164
- All right. Strike two.
- Play ball!

518
00:34:04,919 --> 00:34:06,546
You lost, Launchie?

519
00:34:07,463 --> 00:34:08,464
I'm Ender Wiggin.

520
00:34:11,551 --> 00:34:13,344
Supposed to report to Bonzo Madrid.

521
00:34:13,427 --> 00:34:14,845
So you're the replacement?

522
00:34:15,179 --> 00:34:17,348
- Ender Wiggin.
- Petra Arkanian.

523
00:34:17,431 --> 00:34:19,475
Only girl in the Salamander Army.

524
00:34:19,559 --> 00:34:21,269
With more balls than anybody
else in this bunkroom.

525
00:34:22,061 --> 00:34:24,021
Mama Petra, she talking!

526
00:34:25,982 --> 00:34:26,983
Wiggin?

527
00:34:27,066 --> 00:34:29,193
Sir, yes, sir! Ender Wiggin. Reassigned.

528
00:34:30,319 --> 00:34:31,988
I ask for a replacement for O'Reilly

529
00:34:32,029 --> 00:34:33,322
and this is what I get?

530
00:34:33,573 --> 00:34:37,076
A useless, skinny, untrained snot!

531
00:34:37,159 --> 00:34:39,036
- I'm a quick study.
- Let me be clear.

532
00:34:39,161 --> 00:34:41,664
I intend to trade you ASAP.

533
00:34:42,123 --> 00:34:45,543
My army is undefeated
in the last 21 battles.

534
00:34:45,626 --> 00:34:47,503
I'm on track to make it to Command School

535
00:34:47,795 --> 00:34:48,963
within six months.

536
00:34:49,005 --> 00:34:51,215
You can get your training
at someone else's expense.

537
00:34:51,549 --> 00:34:53,050
- He's all heart.
- Shut it, Petra!

538
00:34:53,134 --> 00:34:54,176
Easy, Bonzo...

539
00:34:54,468 --> 00:34:55,720
Watch your mouth, Dink.

540
00:34:57,972 --> 00:34:59,473
Here's the deal, snot.

541
00:34:59,515 --> 00:35:00,600
When we go into battle,

542
00:35:00,683 --> 00:35:01,976
you will not pass through the gates

543
00:35:02,018 --> 00:35:04,061
until all my soldiers are through.

544
00:35:04,145 --> 00:35:06,939
Then you will remain just inside the gate

545
00:35:07,023 --> 00:35:09,567
with your weapon undrawn and unfired,

546
00:35:09,650 --> 00:35:10,735
until the game ends.

547
00:35:10,818 --> 00:35:12,111
So, I am to do nothing?

548
00:35:12,194 --> 00:35:14,030
You are to keep out of the way.

549
00:35:14,071 --> 00:35:16,157
You bunk at the back of the room.

550
00:35:36,093 --> 00:35:38,054
You know, Bonzo doesn't like to lose.

551
00:35:38,512 --> 00:35:40,097
He doesn't want an untrained Launchie

552
00:35:40,181 --> 00:35:41,641
screwing up his perfect maneuvers.

553
00:35:42,058 --> 00:35:44,101
But the Battle Room is open 24/7.

554
00:35:44,185 --> 00:35:46,646
During free time,
I could show you some moves.

555
00:36:09,794 --> 00:36:11,045
You ready?

556
00:36:13,214 --> 00:36:16,092
In three, two, one...

557
00:36:55,506 --> 00:36:56,507
Impressive.

558
00:36:57,133 --> 00:36:58,300
Your turn.

559
00:37:06,851 --> 00:37:08,853
Okay, you can't just keep
your thumb on the trigger.

560
00:37:08,936 --> 00:37:10,604
You need half a second to recharge.

561
00:37:10,813 --> 00:37:12,314
At least you don't have any bad habits.

562
00:37:12,648 --> 00:37:14,400
I don't have any good ones either.

563
00:37:14,483 --> 00:37:15,484
I'll give you those.

564
00:37:22,450 --> 00:37:23,534
Relax.

565
00:37:23,617 --> 00:37:24,618
The further your target,

566
00:37:24,660 --> 00:37:26,245
the longer you have to hold the beam.

567
00:37:26,328 --> 00:37:27,496
Fire.

568
00:37:32,418 --> 00:37:33,711
Even longer.

569
00:37:35,004 --> 00:37:37,131
It's the difference between
a tenth and a half-second.

570
00:37:37,173 --> 00:37:38,799
But in battle that's a long time.

571
00:37:38,924 --> 00:37:41,343
Aim, fire, hold, recharge.

572
00:37:43,345 --> 00:37:44,472
That's it.

573
00:37:45,014 --> 00:37:46,515
Learn where your trigger actually fires,

574
00:37:46,557 --> 00:37:47,808
and ride the edge.

575
00:37:49,518 --> 00:37:51,479
Now you're gettin' it!

576
00:37:52,021 --> 00:37:55,065
In three, two, one...

577
00:37:55,316 --> 00:37:57,318
Go! Let's see who'll beat me!

578
00:37:57,526 --> 00:37:58,694
Come on, Dink! You can do it!

579
00:37:58,736 --> 00:37:59,945
Once. Just beat me once!

580
00:38:00,112 --> 00:38:01,113
- It's over.
- Come on.

581
00:38:01,197 --> 00:38:02,198
- You can do it.
- You got this!

582
00:38:02,323 --> 00:38:03,491
That's five in a row!

583
00:38:03,866 --> 00:38:05,868
- Who's the boss?
- You the boss, Bonzo.

584
00:38:06,035 --> 00:38:08,078
That's right. I'm the boss. Let's go again.

585
00:38:08,162 --> 00:38:09,455
I'm gonna make this six. Ready?

586
00:38:09,538 --> 00:38:10,873
You'll get better with practice.

587
00:38:10,915 --> 00:38:12,374
Yeah, let's do it again sometime.

588
00:38:13,501 --> 00:38:14,752
That was fun.

589
00:38:19,381 --> 00:38:21,050
- Where were you?
- Practicing.

590
00:38:21,091 --> 00:38:22,218
In free time.

591
00:38:22,259 --> 00:38:23,385
You don't practice with her.

592
00:38:24,220 --> 00:38:25,930
In fact, you don't practice at all!

593
00:38:29,934 --> 00:38:32,645
May I speak to you privately, sir?

594
00:38:37,900 --> 00:38:38,901
Hey...

595
00:38:39,610 --> 00:38:40,611
Wiggin!

596
00:38:41,612 --> 00:38:43,197
Hey! Pendejo!

597
00:38:43,239 --> 00:38:44,907
Don't you ever turn your back on me!

598
00:38:44,990 --> 00:38:46,867
If I'm gonna be useful in this
toon, I have to practice!

599
00:38:46,909 --> 00:38:47,910
You will do what I tell you!

600
00:38:47,993 --> 00:38:50,162
I will follow all commands
you are authorized to give.

601
00:38:50,246 --> 00:38:51,664
But if you take away my free time,

602
00:38:51,747 --> 00:38:52,748
I will get you iced.

603
00:38:57,169 --> 00:38:59,088
Are you threatening me, snot?

604
00:39:01,423 --> 00:39:02,633
No.

605
00:39:03,926 --> 00:39:07,263
Listen. I know you want to trade me.

606
00:39:07,346 --> 00:39:08,973
But no one will take me
if I don't know anything.

607
00:39:10,015 --> 00:39:11,976
Let me practice.
You can get rid of me sooner.

608
00:39:12,142 --> 00:39:13,602
I already gave you an order!

609
00:39:13,769 --> 00:39:15,271
I know. In front of everybody.

610
00:39:15,354 --> 00:39:16,438
And you don't want your soldiers to think

611
00:39:16,480 --> 00:39:17,481
that you backed down.

612
00:39:17,565 --> 00:39:20,568
So, for tonight, you can say
that you won this argument.

613
00:39:20,609 --> 00:39:21,777
Then tomorrow, you can tell everybody

614
00:39:21,819 --> 00:39:23,362
that you changed your mind.

615
00:39:23,445 --> 00:39:24,947
You'll look generous, I'll get to train,

616
00:39:24,989 --> 00:39:26,949
we both win. Deal?

617
00:39:28,325 --> 00:39:30,452
You'd better watch your back, Wiggin.

618
00:39:44,884 --> 00:39:46,635
Wake up!

619
00:39:47,303 --> 00:39:48,387
Wake up, mis pendejos!

620
00:39:48,637 --> 00:39:50,931
Battle with Leopard in 10 minutes!

621
00:39:50,973 --> 00:39:52,725
- Hey, Wiggin!
- Yes, sir!

622
00:39:52,975 --> 00:39:54,184
I changed my mind.

623
00:39:56,270 --> 00:39:58,647
Maybe by watching my toons,
you'll learn something

624
00:39:58,689 --> 00:40:00,649
and I can trade you easier.

625
00:40:00,733 --> 00:40:02,651
Yes, sir. Thank you, sir!

626
00:40:02,735 --> 00:40:05,362
Move! Everybody, let's move!

627
00:40:05,487 --> 00:40:08,324
Salamander is number one

628
00:40:08,365 --> 00:40:10,659
Salamander is number one

629
00:40:10,701 --> 00:40:13,203
There's no one like us under the sun

630
00:40:13,287 --> 00:40:16,165
There's no one like us under the sun

631
00:40:16,206 --> 00:40:19,084
'Cause Salamanders, we're on top

632
00:40:19,168 --> 00:40:21,378
'Cause Salamanders, we're on top

633
00:40:21,462 --> 00:40:23,881
When it comes to winning, we never stop

634
00:40:23,964 --> 00:40:26,800
When it comes to winning, we never stop

635
00:40:27,343 --> 00:40:28,510
Salamander halt!

636
00:40:29,678 --> 00:40:31,347
At ease.

637
00:40:32,389 --> 00:40:33,390
What's the play?

638
00:40:33,474 --> 00:40:35,184
Four winds. Toon A, up,

639
00:40:35,225 --> 00:40:37,478
B left, C right, D down.

640
00:40:39,021 --> 00:40:42,149
You, Wiggin. You hang back near the gate.

641
00:40:42,191 --> 00:40:44,193
Bonzo, my toon'll be a man
short without him.

642
00:40:44,234 --> 00:40:46,195
He knows nothing about
our formations, Dink.

643
00:40:46,278 --> 00:40:47,988
He'll only get in the way.

644
00:40:48,030 --> 00:40:49,406
You come out last.

645
00:40:49,531 --> 00:40:51,867
Hang back and observe. We don't need you.

646
00:40:53,327 --> 00:40:54,328
Step aside.

647
00:40:57,831 --> 00:41:00,209
Go, Salamander! Go! Go! Go! Go!

648
00:41:00,292 --> 00:41:02,878
Go, go Salamander! Go! Go!

649
00:41:36,578 --> 00:41:37,788
We gotta break them up.

650
00:41:37,997 --> 00:41:40,416
Fly, you lock with me. Petra rides chariot!

651
00:41:40,457 --> 00:41:41,542
- Got it?
- Got it!

652
00:41:41,583 --> 00:41:42,751
- Ready?
- Ready.

653
00:41:42,835 --> 00:41:45,587
In three, two, one...

654
00:41:59,810 --> 00:42:01,103
- I'm hit!
- Me too!

655
00:42:01,145 --> 00:42:02,813
Keep shooting, Petra!

656
00:42:03,355 --> 00:42:04,356
Body hit her!

657
00:42:04,440 --> 00:42:05,983
- Take her out! Go!
- I'm on it!

658
00:42:29,882 --> 00:42:30,883
Wiggin!

659
00:42:30,966 --> 00:42:32,968
What are you doin'? I
told you to stay back!

660
00:42:41,393 --> 00:42:42,478
Are you okay?

661
00:42:42,561 --> 00:42:43,979
What are you doing here?
Bonzo will kill you.

662
00:42:44,063 --> 00:42:45,230
I can't go back now.

663
00:42:45,314 --> 00:42:46,648
Well, then get in the game. We're losing.

664
00:42:47,983 --> 00:42:50,152
They've got half their
toon back near their gate.

665
00:42:50,486 --> 00:42:52,821
Put your feet to mine. Redirect me.

666
00:42:52,863 --> 00:42:53,864
Play dead.

667
00:42:53,947 --> 00:42:55,616
Don't draw your weapon
till you know you have a shot.

668
00:42:55,657 --> 00:42:56,658
Got it.

669
00:42:58,035 --> 00:43:00,996
In three, two, one...

670
00:44:14,361 --> 00:44:16,655
Smart move, holding Wiggin back.

671
00:44:42,431 --> 00:44:43,599
Where'd you learn all this?

672
00:44:43,849 --> 00:44:44,892
I had a brother.

673
00:44:45,267 --> 00:44:46,935
- Had?
- Have.

674
00:44:48,061 --> 00:44:49,104
Come on. Let's go again.

675
00:44:49,813 --> 00:44:51,773
But use your arms, not your hips.

676
00:44:53,609 --> 00:44:56,069
Officer on deck! A-ten-hut!

677
00:44:59,281 --> 00:45:01,033
I thought I told you not to train with her.

678
00:45:01,491 --> 00:45:04,203
I thought we'd agreed
that free time was free, sir.

679
00:45:05,829 --> 00:45:06,830
At ease.

680
00:45:10,667 --> 00:45:11,960
Stop it, Bonzo!

681
00:45:13,962 --> 00:45:16,256
Try making me look like a fool again

682
00:45:16,298 --> 00:45:17,466
and I'll kill you.

683
00:45:28,185 --> 00:45:29,436
Are you okay?

684
00:45:30,896 --> 00:45:31,897
Yeah.

685
00:46:35,252 --> 00:46:36,878
What do you want me to do?

686
00:46:43,051 --> 00:46:44,261
Valentine?

687
00:46:48,098 --> 00:46:49,558
How can you be in my game?

688
00:48:31,326 --> 00:48:32,327
Well done.

689
00:48:32,411 --> 00:48:33,412
You're a killer now.

690
00:48:36,998 --> 00:48:38,500
Nightmares, Launchie?

691
00:48:38,834 --> 00:48:40,502
Keep 'em to yourself.

692
00:48:41,753 --> 00:48:45,424
You said the game would
reveal his state of mind,

693
00:48:45,507 --> 00:48:46,883
not screw with it!

694
00:48:47,092 --> 00:48:50,178
How did his psycho brother
end up in the game?

695
00:48:50,262 --> 00:48:52,347
He's obviously feeling
some psychological pressure...

696
00:48:52,431 --> 00:48:54,349
Of course he's feeling pressure, Anderson!

697
00:48:54,391 --> 00:48:56,435
This is a boot camp for kids

698
00:48:56,518 --> 00:48:58,645
that are gonna have to face a real enemy!

699
00:48:58,728 --> 00:49:00,439
The game is a thought relationship

700
00:49:00,522 --> 00:49:02,232
between the child and the computer.

701
00:49:02,315 --> 00:49:03,733
Together they create stories.

702
00:49:03,900 --> 00:49:06,027
Then change the story!

703
00:49:06,111 --> 00:49:08,071
The stories reflect
the child's emotional reality.

704
00:49:08,155 --> 00:49:09,197
I can't change that!

705
00:49:09,531 --> 00:49:12,200
I don't know how these images
got into the game.

706
00:49:14,411 --> 00:49:16,037
Erase the game.

707
00:49:43,482 --> 00:49:44,483
Doin' well.

708
00:49:46,568 --> 00:49:47,569
Very well.

709
00:49:48,153 --> 00:49:49,654
Top test scores in class.

710
00:49:50,071 --> 00:49:51,907
Highest Battle Room ratings.

711
00:49:51,990 --> 00:49:54,534
But you have a habit
of upsetting your commander.

712
00:49:54,618 --> 00:49:56,244
I find it hard to respect someone

713
00:49:56,328 --> 00:49:58,079
just because they outrank me, sir.

714
00:49:58,121 --> 00:50:00,290
Puts you in a difficult
position, doesn't it?

715
00:50:00,373 --> 00:50:01,374
Yes, sir.

716
00:50:02,083 --> 00:50:04,377
You don't like taking orders from Bonzo.

717
00:50:04,586 --> 00:50:05,754
No, sir.

718
00:50:06,505 --> 00:50:09,174
Perhaps you'd prefer to give them yourself?

719
00:50:09,841 --> 00:50:10,842
Sir?

720
00:50:10,926 --> 00:50:13,512
How would you like to lead your own army?

721
00:50:13,595 --> 00:50:14,596
Dragon Army.

722
00:50:15,347 --> 00:50:17,307
Sir, I've never heard of a Dragon Army.

723
00:50:17,432 --> 00:50:20,060
We discontinued the name four years ago.

724
00:50:21,102 --> 00:50:23,104
No Dragon Army ever won a battle.

725
00:50:23,647 --> 00:50:25,440
Then why not a new name, sir?

726
00:50:25,524 --> 00:50:27,692
Because we already have the uniforms.

727
00:50:29,152 --> 00:50:30,862
And who will be in this army, sir?

728
00:50:30,946 --> 00:50:33,031
Misfits. Like you.

729
00:50:33,114 --> 00:50:35,617
Oddballs who might just be brilliant

730
00:50:35,700 --> 00:50:37,202
with the right commander.

731
00:50:40,872 --> 00:50:42,332
Your new quarters.

732
00:50:51,800 --> 00:50:53,677
Your soldiers are being notified now.

733
00:50:53,760 --> 00:50:55,470
You will address them in 15 minutes.

734
00:50:57,973 --> 00:50:59,432
Do you think they'll follow me?

735
00:51:41,850 --> 00:51:43,518
A-ten-hut!

736
00:51:43,727 --> 00:51:45,020
Officer on deck.

737
00:51:47,355 --> 00:51:48,356
At ease.

738
00:51:49,190 --> 00:51:50,900
Welcome to Dragon Army.

739
00:51:50,984 --> 00:51:52,652
Bunking will be arranged
with youngest at the front

740
00:51:52,694 --> 00:51:53,695
and veterans at the back.

741
00:51:54,029 --> 00:51:55,030
Ender,

742
00:51:55,739 --> 00:51:58,033
every other commander has their seniors
closest to the door.

743
00:51:58,074 --> 00:52:00,285
Well, I don't intend to be
like every other commander.

744
00:52:00,452 --> 00:52:03,204
What am I doing here, Ender?
You don't even like me.

745
00:52:03,371 --> 00:52:04,914
I didn't select this army, Bernard.

746
00:52:04,998 --> 00:52:08,001
But I intend to make it
the best in this school.

747
00:52:08,543 --> 00:52:10,378
I think you can help make that happen.

748
00:52:12,631 --> 00:52:13,923
Am I wrong?

749
00:52:14,883 --> 00:52:15,884
No, sir.

750
00:52:17,052 --> 00:52:18,720
You will respect one another.

751
00:52:18,762 --> 00:52:21,139
If anybody has an idea they
think is better than mine,

752
00:52:21,222 --> 00:52:22,265
I wanna hear it.

753
00:52:22,474 --> 00:52:24,225
I can't be expected to do all the thinking

754
00:52:24,309 --> 00:52:25,435
in this army, can I, Bean?

755
00:52:25,935 --> 00:52:28,396
- No, sir!
- Then let's get suited up.

756
00:52:28,438 --> 00:52:30,649
- Training starts now!
- Sir, yes, sir!

757
00:52:43,453 --> 00:52:44,996
He's pushing them hard.

758
00:52:45,080 --> 00:52:46,915
Might even make something of Bernard.

759
00:52:46,998 --> 00:52:49,584
Command School is pressing for a decision.

760
00:52:51,878 --> 00:52:53,755
Tell them we need more time.

761
00:52:55,340 --> 00:52:56,925
We're out of time.

762
00:52:57,759 --> 00:52:58,927
Lieutenant.

763
00:52:59,010 --> 00:53:01,429
Tomorrow's game will commence at 0300.

764
00:53:01,471 --> 00:53:02,681
Yes, sir.

765
00:53:17,445 --> 00:53:18,655
Wake up! Wake up!

766
00:53:18,738 --> 00:53:21,491
Battle with Salamander and Leopard!
In five!

767
00:53:21,616 --> 00:53:22,951
Two armies at once?

768
00:53:22,992 --> 00:53:24,452
The Colonel is changing the rules!

769
00:53:24,536 --> 00:53:26,538
In a battle with the Formics,
there will be no rules.

770
00:53:28,832 --> 00:53:29,833
You all right?

771
00:53:30,667 --> 00:53:31,668
I twisted my ankle.

772
00:53:31,876 --> 00:53:34,295
- How bad?
- Not good.

773
00:53:34,337 --> 00:53:35,714
Dink, get him to the infirmary.

774
00:53:35,797 --> 00:53:38,466
The rest of you, let's move!
Come on! We're late! Come on!

775
00:53:50,186 --> 00:53:51,479
They already opened the gate?

776
00:54:08,371 --> 00:54:09,497
Petra?

777
00:54:09,539 --> 00:54:10,832
Two armies weren't enough?

778
00:54:10,874 --> 00:54:12,167
They had to block your view too?

779
00:54:12,375 --> 00:54:13,543
What are you doing here?

780
00:54:13,668 --> 00:54:15,462
Colonel said you needed a sub.

781
00:54:15,503 --> 00:54:16,588
Guess he thought your odds were zero

782
00:54:16,671 --> 00:54:17,672
with me on the other team.

783
00:54:18,089 --> 00:54:19,424
Bonzo agree to this?

784
00:54:19,507 --> 00:54:21,509
- Colonel Graff's orders.
- He didn't have a choice.

785
00:54:22,886 --> 00:54:24,387
Dink. Kneel.

786
00:54:24,721 --> 00:54:27,348
- What?
- I have an idea. Kneel.

787
00:54:29,851 --> 00:54:30,977
Ready?

788
00:54:31,186 --> 00:54:33,855
In three, two,

789
00:54:33,938 --> 00:54:36,149
- one!
- Fire now!

790
00:54:36,524 --> 00:54:38,234
Shoot 'em! Fire!

791
00:54:52,123 --> 00:54:53,291
Look out!

792
00:54:54,292 --> 00:54:55,919
Twelve clear on the wall!

793
00:54:56,002 --> 00:54:57,420
Twelve down, 20 to go.

794
00:54:57,545 --> 00:54:59,214
They could be right behind
these forward stars

795
00:54:59,255 --> 00:55:00,465
or all the way back at their gate.

796
00:55:04,052 --> 00:55:05,720
- Ready?
- Ready.

797
00:55:24,113 --> 00:55:25,114
Now!

798
00:55:26,324 --> 00:55:27,700
Pull!

799
00:55:41,840 --> 00:55:43,591
Dumbos have a bunch of stars
around their gate

800
00:55:43,633 --> 00:55:44,968
like a giant donut!

801
00:55:45,051 --> 00:55:46,052
They're just hanging behind 'em.

802
00:55:46,094 --> 00:55:47,887
- No one closer?
- Nah.

803
00:55:48,721 --> 00:55:49,889
Nice.

804
00:55:50,265 --> 00:55:51,850
Let's see how they handle a formation.

805
00:55:51,933 --> 00:55:53,101
We've never done a formation.

806
00:55:53,184 --> 00:55:54,644
Then they won't expect one.

807
00:56:02,485 --> 00:56:03,945
We still outnumber him.

808
00:56:04,028 --> 00:56:05,446
We should storm him and crush him.

809
00:56:05,488 --> 00:56:08,741
No. We hold our positions.
He has to come to us.

810
00:56:08,783 --> 00:56:09,868
We can't lose.

811
00:56:19,127 --> 00:56:20,628
Open fire!

812
00:56:23,840 --> 00:56:25,133
They're drifting upwards!

813
00:56:25,300 --> 00:56:27,427
On my count, row two, push row one!

814
00:56:27,468 --> 00:56:29,554
We're changing direction, 30 degrees!

815
00:56:29,637 --> 00:56:31,556
In three, two, one...

816
00:56:31,806 --> 00:56:32,807
Now!

817
00:56:33,057 --> 00:56:35,643
Rear thrusters, row six... Now!

818
00:56:36,060 --> 00:56:37,812
Row five... Now!

819
00:56:38,187 --> 00:56:39,731
Come on. Don't let them through.

820
00:56:39,814 --> 00:56:40,982
We've gotta break them up!

821
00:56:41,149 --> 00:56:42,901
We're almost there!

822
00:56:45,904 --> 00:56:47,071
- I'm hit!
- Hold on!

823
00:56:47,155 --> 00:56:48,156
Alai, are you okay?

824
00:56:48,239 --> 00:56:50,491
- Yeah! Are we there yet?
- Almost! Keep close!

825
00:56:50,575 --> 00:56:53,494
- Alai can't get hit!
- We're nearly there!

826
00:56:53,661 --> 00:56:55,330
Keep shooting!

827
00:57:00,835 --> 00:57:03,212
We did it! Yeah!

828
00:57:03,296 --> 00:57:05,840
Eat that! Dragon rules! Yes!

829
00:57:06,341 --> 00:57:08,384
- Who's undefeated now?
- Dragon!

830
00:57:09,594 --> 00:57:11,346
Still think he's not ready?

831
00:57:12,847 --> 00:57:14,182
Don't be smug.

832
00:57:14,265 --> 00:57:15,475
Yeah!

833
00:57:15,516 --> 00:57:18,519
Did you see the look on Bonzo's face?

834
00:57:43,711 --> 00:57:44,879
We're tired of you, Ender.

835
00:57:45,296 --> 00:57:46,839
You know, your father would be proud.

836
00:57:47,173 --> 00:57:48,883
Come to fight a boy in the shower.

837
00:57:48,925 --> 00:57:50,009
With your buddies.

838
00:57:53,096 --> 00:57:54,472
Go watch the door.

839
00:57:56,057 --> 00:57:57,266
Go!

840
00:58:08,611 --> 00:58:10,154
Look...

841
00:58:10,238 --> 00:58:11,906
You can say you won.

842
00:58:12,615 --> 00:58:13,950
I'll say you taught me a lesson.

843
00:58:14,075 --> 00:58:15,368
No, coward.

844
00:58:16,077 --> 00:58:17,245
Raise your fists.

845
00:58:18,329 --> 00:58:20,456
Come out and fight! Come on!

846
00:58:21,082 --> 00:58:23,084
Come on, fight! Come on!

847
00:58:32,593 --> 00:58:34,637
I could break your arm!

848
00:58:45,440 --> 00:58:46,441
Bonzo?

849
00:58:49,277 --> 00:58:50,278
Bonzo!

850
00:58:50,695 --> 00:58:51,988
Bonzo?

851
00:58:52,488 --> 00:58:53,489
Help!

852
00:58:54,032 --> 00:58:56,117
We need help in here!

853
00:59:06,836 --> 00:59:08,838
Everybody knows he started it.

854
00:59:13,509 --> 00:59:14,761
Ender...

855
00:59:14,802 --> 00:59:16,471
- I am so sorry...
- Major!

856
00:59:19,849 --> 00:59:21,476
We should never have
allowed you to be alone...

857
00:59:21,559 --> 00:59:23,269
Not now, Major!

858
00:59:24,145 --> 00:59:25,354
Leave us.

859
00:59:33,362 --> 00:59:34,655
Leave him.

860
00:59:34,864 --> 00:59:35,865
Now.

861
00:59:37,700 --> 00:59:38,951
You too, cadet.

862
01:00:01,516 --> 01:00:03,309
He's gonna die, isn't he?

863
01:00:05,019 --> 01:00:07,355
No... No.

864
01:00:08,731 --> 01:00:09,899
Please, don't lie to me.

865
01:00:11,150 --> 01:00:14,028
We're gonna send him home. Back to Earth.

866
01:00:14,862 --> 01:00:16,656
So he can get better.

867
01:00:17,532 --> 01:00:18,574
I want to go with him.

868
01:00:18,658 --> 01:00:20,118
I can't let you go.

869
01:00:20,910 --> 01:00:21,953
You've come so far.

870
01:00:22,036 --> 01:00:23,496
And I wanna talk to my sister.

871
01:00:24,580 --> 01:00:27,083
The Fleet owns you, Ender.

872
01:00:28,167 --> 01:00:30,378
Strategos would never allow it.

873
01:00:31,087 --> 01:00:34,882
Send me home, Colonel, or I will resign.

874
01:00:37,718 --> 01:00:39,554
Don't threaten me, boy.

875
01:00:41,264 --> 01:00:43,224
I am not the enemy.

876
01:00:47,728 --> 01:00:49,230
I'm not so sure.

877
01:00:53,901 --> 01:00:56,195
I won't play this game anymore.

878
01:00:59,532 --> 01:01:00,533
I quit.

879
01:01:04,078 --> 01:01:05,454
What are you gonna do?

880
01:01:06,873 --> 01:01:08,749
Waste millions on a loser?

881
01:01:16,841 --> 01:01:18,176
You wanted to see me.

882
01:01:18,384 --> 01:01:19,844
You can't resign.

883
01:01:19,927 --> 01:01:22,096
You have an obligation to stay here

884
01:01:22,138 --> 01:01:23,890
and convince him to do his duty.

885
01:01:24,223 --> 01:01:25,266
My father trained horses.

886
01:01:25,600 --> 01:01:27,935
I've raised yearlings
since I was five years old.

887
01:01:28,019 --> 01:01:29,729
I know a thoroughbred when I see one.

888
01:01:29,770 --> 01:01:31,063
We can't lose him.

889
01:01:31,272 --> 01:01:32,607
My God...

890
01:01:32,690 --> 01:01:34,734
You really don't see them
as children, do you?

891
01:01:34,942 --> 01:01:36,194
It used to be a war crime

892
01:01:36,277 --> 01:01:38,196
to recruit anyone under the age of 15.

893
01:01:38,279 --> 01:01:40,448
When the war is over,
we can have the luxury

894
01:01:40,489 --> 01:01:42,450
of debating the morality of what we do.

895
01:01:42,617 --> 01:01:44,410
When it's over, what
will be left of the boy?

896
01:01:44,493 --> 01:01:46,412
What does it matter if
there's nothing left at all?

897
01:01:47,413 --> 01:01:49,415
We're using these children to win a war.

898
01:01:51,292 --> 01:01:52,460
And if they come home,

899
01:01:52,543 --> 01:01:54,795
it's my job to put them
back together again.

900
01:02:04,180 --> 01:02:05,640
Thanks for what you've done.

901
01:02:43,803 --> 01:02:45,846
- Where's Ender?
- Hello, Valentine.

902
01:02:46,138 --> 01:02:47,682
Why are you here? Did something happen?

903
01:02:47,848 --> 01:02:49,183
They won't let me see him.

904
01:02:49,684 --> 01:02:51,560
I need you to take a ride with me.

905
01:03:00,319 --> 01:03:02,446
He's gonna be happy to see you.

906
01:03:03,531 --> 01:03:05,658
Come on. You just want him to re-enlist.

907
01:03:05,741 --> 01:03:07,243
I want him to save lives.

908
01:03:07,493 --> 01:03:09,537
And what about his life?

909
01:03:47,199 --> 01:03:49,076
I've been sitting by Bonzo's bed,

910
01:03:49,827 --> 01:03:51,579
waiting for him to wake up.

911
01:03:53,122 --> 01:03:54,874
But he may never wake up.

912
01:03:55,333 --> 01:03:57,084
Ender, he attacked first.

913
01:03:57,293 --> 01:04:00,254
And I fought back, just
like Peter taught me.

914
01:04:01,547 --> 01:04:03,841
I've had a lot of fights, Val.

915
01:04:04,633 --> 01:04:06,552
I've won because I've always understood

916
01:04:06,594 --> 01:04:08,095
the way my enemy thinks.

917
01:04:08,387 --> 01:04:09,972
And when I truly understand them...

918
01:04:10,056 --> 01:04:11,223
You also love them.

919
01:04:14,727 --> 01:04:17,897
I think it's impossible
to truly understand someone

920
01:04:18,314 --> 01:04:20,441
and not love them
the way they love themselves.

921
01:04:20,733 --> 01:04:22,485
- But in that moment...
- You beat them.

922
01:04:22,693 --> 01:04:24,278
I destroy them.

923
01:04:25,237 --> 01:04:27,656
I make it impossible for them
to ever hurt me again.

924
01:04:32,244 --> 01:04:34,497
Ender, they want me to talk
you into going back.

925
01:04:35,456 --> 01:04:37,291
I told them I won't cooperate.

926
01:04:37,333 --> 01:04:38,584
I don't think you're hiding here

927
01:04:38,626 --> 01:04:40,252
just because you care about Bonzo.

928
01:04:40,878 --> 01:04:43,089
I think you're hiding
because you're afraid.

929
01:04:44,507 --> 01:04:46,342
Afraid you don't know your enemy.

930
01:04:46,884 --> 01:04:48,386
Afraid you might lose.

931
01:04:48,469 --> 01:04:50,304
But what if you're the next Mazer Rackham?

932
01:04:52,181 --> 01:04:54,433
You can't hide here forever.

933
01:04:56,435 --> 01:04:58,020
But if you stay here,

934
01:04:59,730 --> 01:05:01,440
if you don't try,

935
01:05:02,149 --> 01:05:04,276
then we will all be lost.

936
01:05:14,620 --> 01:05:15,996
I'll miss you.

937
01:05:18,707 --> 01:05:20,626
I'll miss you, too.

938
01:05:41,188 --> 01:05:43,732
I need to know that you will
not block my e-mails again.

939
01:05:48,028 --> 01:05:49,238
Attention,

940
01:05:49,321 --> 01:05:53,075
prepare for transporter docking operation.

941
01:05:53,159 --> 01:05:55,369
Initiating final approach.

942
01:05:57,204 --> 01:05:59,081
I thought we were going back
to Battle School.

943
01:05:59,165 --> 01:06:01,208
- We're not.
- Where are we going?

944
01:06:03,252 --> 01:06:04,628
Much further.

945
01:06:13,679 --> 01:06:15,139
"Dear Valentine,

946
01:06:15,222 --> 01:06:17,558
"I must now travel
to our advanced command base

947
01:06:17,600 --> 01:06:19,226
"near the Formics' home planet,

948
01:06:19,310 --> 01:06:21,562
"where I'll begin final training.

949
01:06:21,604 --> 01:06:25,566
"If successful, I'll command
the entire invasion fleet.

950
01:06:26,066 --> 01:06:30,154
"I wish there was another way,
but war seems inevitable.

951
01:06:30,529 --> 01:06:33,449
"Stay safe. Love, Ender."

952
01:07:48,732 --> 01:07:50,484
Not very hospitable, is it?

953
01:07:50,693 --> 01:07:51,902
We took it from the Formics

954
01:07:51,986 --> 01:07:54,488
27 years after Rackham's victory.

955
01:07:54,822 --> 01:07:56,156
Flushed them out of these tunnels

956
01:07:56,240 --> 01:07:57,783
like rats from a sewer.

957
01:07:58,867 --> 01:08:00,995
Drove 'em all the way back
to their home planet.

958
01:08:01,036 --> 01:08:03,247
- How long did they live here?
- We're not sure.

959
01:08:03,330 --> 01:08:05,082
This was a forward staging post

960
01:08:05,165 --> 01:08:06,500
for their invasion of Earth.

961
01:08:06,667 --> 01:08:09,878
We built our base here to be
closer to their home planet,

962
01:08:09,962 --> 01:08:11,755
to allow instantaneous communication

963
01:08:11,839 --> 01:08:13,507
by Ansible with our attack fleet.

964
01:08:13,549 --> 01:08:14,800
If they're on their home planet,

965
01:08:14,842 --> 01:08:15,884
do we have them contained?

966
01:08:16,051 --> 01:08:17,052
For now.

967
01:08:17,136 --> 01:08:19,513
If we have them boxed in, why go to war?

968
01:08:20,222 --> 01:08:23,434
For the same reason that
you kept kicking that bully

969
01:08:23,517 --> 01:08:25,352
before I recruited you.

970
01:08:25,644 --> 01:08:29,565
The purpose of this war
is to prevent all future wars.

971
01:08:30,274 --> 01:08:33,110
Your training begins
first thing tomorrow morning.

972
01:08:33,444 --> 01:08:36,488
Sergeant Dap will show you
to your quarters.

973
01:08:38,782 --> 01:08:39,783
Yes, sir.

974
01:08:49,293 --> 01:08:51,211
We're still re-seeding the atmosphere.

975
01:08:51,295 --> 01:08:53,172
It's breathable, but thin.

976
01:08:53,213 --> 01:08:54,715
In the event of an evacuation,

977
01:08:54,757 --> 01:08:56,383
two breaths every minute from one of these

978
01:08:56,467 --> 01:08:58,594
will compensate for lower
levels of surface oxygen.

979
01:08:59,762 --> 01:09:01,221
Lights out in five.

980
01:10:12,793 --> 01:10:13,794
Who are you?

981
01:10:19,591 --> 01:10:20,676
Look, this may be amusing to you,

982
01:10:20,759 --> 01:10:21,969
but they'll come looking for me.

983
01:10:26,849 --> 01:10:28,976
You wanna fight me? Is that the test?

984
01:10:29,268 --> 01:10:31,145
To see if I'll attack an old man?

985
01:10:32,062 --> 01:10:33,397
Well, I won't.

986
01:10:37,735 --> 01:10:39,611
I'll just sit this one out.

987
01:10:46,785 --> 01:10:47,953
Okay. You win.

988
01:10:47,995 --> 01:10:50,664
Since when do you tell
the enemy when he has won?

989
01:10:50,748 --> 01:10:51,790
I surprised you once.

990
01:10:51,832 --> 01:10:53,959
Why didn't you destroy me
immediately after?

991
01:10:54,084 --> 01:10:55,335
I thought you were a teacher.

992
01:10:55,502 --> 01:10:57,171
There is no teacher but the enemy.

993
01:10:57,671 --> 01:10:59,798
Only he will tell you where you are weak,

994
01:10:59,840 --> 01:11:01,133
where he is strong.

995
01:11:01,175 --> 01:11:04,011
From now on, I am your enemy, got it?

996
01:11:05,471 --> 01:11:07,890
- Yes.
- Good.

997
01:11:15,230 --> 01:11:18,025
During training, I will devise
the strategy of your enemy.

998
01:11:18,108 --> 01:11:19,651
Remember, he is stronger than you.

999
01:11:19,693 --> 01:11:21,528
From now on, you are always about to lose.

1000
01:11:25,532 --> 01:11:26,784
Sir?

1001
01:11:29,787 --> 01:11:31,163
Do you have a name?

1002
01:11:32,414 --> 01:11:33,540
Mazer Rackham.

1003
01:11:35,876 --> 01:11:38,212
What? You thought I was dead?

1004
01:11:38,879 --> 01:11:42,132
Sir, I've been building models
of your planes

1005
01:11:42,216 --> 01:11:43,801
since I was six years old.

1006
01:11:46,595 --> 01:11:48,180
I have a question, sir.

1007
01:11:48,972 --> 01:11:50,516
On the vids,

1008
01:11:50,557 --> 01:11:51,600
they always cut out

1009
01:11:51,683 --> 01:11:53,727
right after you destroy the one carrier.

1010
01:11:55,103 --> 01:11:56,563
Why?

1011
01:11:57,064 --> 01:11:58,565
Get dressed.

1012
01:12:02,820 --> 01:12:04,571
Sir, I've already seen this.

1013
01:12:04,655 --> 01:12:05,864
I wanna know what happens after.

1014
01:12:06,156 --> 01:12:07,157
Just watch.

1015
01:12:25,092 --> 01:12:27,594
After the explosion cleared,

1016
01:12:28,762 --> 01:12:31,765
everything was incredibly still.

1017
01:12:35,185 --> 01:12:37,479
Their ships just stopped shooting.

1018
01:12:38,021 --> 01:12:39,773
And then they started
falling out of the sky.

1019
01:12:48,156 --> 01:12:49,825
Scroll back, please.

1020
01:12:49,950 --> 01:12:52,119
To just after you lost your wing man.

1021
01:12:55,414 --> 01:12:56,415
There.

1022
01:12:56,582 --> 01:12:57,624
Play back, please.

1023
01:13:02,212 --> 01:13:04,256
You took cover in the cloud.

1024
01:13:04,840 --> 01:13:05,966
You couldn't see anything,

1025
01:13:07,217 --> 01:13:08,677
so you must have been using your HUD.

1026
01:13:08,886 --> 01:13:10,220
There. Stop.

1027
01:13:12,431 --> 01:13:13,807
You saw something.

1028
01:13:14,057 --> 01:13:16,643
What did you see in your HUD?
Did you find a pattern?

1029
01:13:16,727 --> 01:13:18,312
Very good, Ender.

1030
01:13:24,902 --> 01:13:26,445
Thermal imaging from a satellite.

1031
01:13:26,778 --> 01:13:29,740
The enemy's in red.
What pattern do you see?

1032
01:13:29,823 --> 01:13:31,074
It seems random.

1033
01:13:31,742 --> 01:13:32,743
But it's not.

1034
01:13:34,411 --> 01:13:37,289
There's an epicenter, right there.

1035
01:13:37,915 --> 01:13:39,124
Meaning?

1036
01:13:39,249 --> 01:13:41,168
You took out that one particular ship,

1037
01:13:41,209 --> 01:13:42,753
and the rest just

1038
01:13:43,253 --> 01:13:44,254
gave up?

1039
01:13:45,547 --> 01:13:46,548
Why?

1040
01:13:50,010 --> 01:13:51,511
To what animals are the Formics

1041
01:13:51,595 --> 01:13:52,846
most often compared?

1042
01:13:53,180 --> 01:13:55,182
- Ants.
- Which have...

1043
01:13:55,766 --> 01:13:57,184
A queen...

1044
01:13:57,851 --> 01:13:59,603
Who directs the worker ants.

1045
01:14:01,772 --> 01:14:04,274
What she thinks, they do.

1046
01:14:04,733 --> 01:14:06,568
Without her, they can't
think for themselves...

1047
01:14:06,860 --> 01:14:08,028
And they die.

1048
01:14:08,153 --> 01:14:09,529
You destroyed the queen's ship.

1049
01:14:09,696 --> 01:14:10,906
I must have. Yes.

1050
01:14:11,198 --> 01:14:13,116
- But you can't be certain?
- No.

1051
01:14:14,034 --> 01:14:16,411
And so the Hegemon insisted
we keep it classified.

1052
01:14:16,578 --> 01:14:18,580
That's why they never show
the rest of the battle.

1053
01:14:18,789 --> 01:14:20,332
Or my face.

1054
01:14:21,124 --> 01:14:22,459
To the world, I'm dead.

1055
01:14:23,543 --> 01:14:24,920
Colonel...

1056
01:14:26,004 --> 01:14:27,047
Your face...

1057
01:14:27,714 --> 01:14:29,174
You mean, why is it marked?

1058
01:14:32,052 --> 01:14:33,887
My father was a Maori.

1059
01:14:35,263 --> 01:14:37,057
Lost him in the war.

1060
01:14:37,766 --> 01:14:41,645
Ta Moko is a way to connect to my past.

1061
01:14:42,646 --> 01:14:44,064
To my inner skin.

1062
01:14:45,273 --> 01:14:47,651
It was a way for me to speak for the dead.

1063
01:14:55,575 --> 01:14:58,078
Sir, have you ever seen a queen?

1064
01:14:58,161 --> 01:14:59,538
No. No one has.

1065
01:14:59,579 --> 01:15:01,289
But if the Formics have
rebuilt their fleet,

1066
01:15:01,373 --> 01:15:03,041
there must be more than one queen.

1067
01:15:03,083 --> 01:15:05,043
Yes, of course. On their home planet.

1068
01:15:05,168 --> 01:15:06,586
What happened when you attacked here?

1069
01:15:07,838 --> 01:15:09,589
- Did you find one?
- No.

1070
01:15:10,173 --> 01:15:11,425
Why did they come?

1071
01:15:11,925 --> 01:15:13,218
Water.

1072
01:15:32,696 --> 01:15:34,448
Attention!

1073
01:15:36,783 --> 01:15:37,951
Officer on deck!

1074
01:15:38,493 --> 01:15:40,537
- Hey, Bean.
- Ho, Commander!

1075
01:15:41,455 --> 01:15:42,497
Petra.

1076
01:15:42,581 --> 01:15:43,665
We thought you were iced.

1077
01:15:43,749 --> 01:15:45,292
We were gonna have to have Dink take over.

1078
01:15:45,375 --> 01:15:46,877
That was never gonna happen!

1079
01:15:47,502 --> 01:15:48,670
Salaam, Alai.

1080
01:15:48,795 --> 01:15:49,796
Salaam, Commander!

1081
01:15:49,838 --> 01:15:51,965
- Bernard.
- Good to see you, sir.

1082
01:15:52,674 --> 01:15:53,800
At ease.

1083
01:15:55,177 --> 01:15:56,636
While you've been skinny-dipping,

1084
01:15:56,678 --> 01:15:58,972
the Colonel's been flogging us
to death on the simulator!

1085
01:15:59,014 --> 01:16:00,015
All right. Take your seats.

1086
01:16:00,807 --> 01:16:01,892
In a matter of weeks,

1087
01:16:01,975 --> 01:16:03,894
we may be called on to fight a real battle.

1088
01:16:03,977 --> 01:16:06,313
Let's bring your commander up to speed.

1089
01:16:07,856 --> 01:16:10,400
Our latest probe images
will give you an idea

1090
01:16:10,484 --> 01:16:12,152
of what's happening on the enemy planet.

1091
01:16:19,659 --> 01:16:22,829
Like us, they appear to have
a population growth rate

1092
01:16:22,871 --> 01:16:24,498
that's unsustainable.

1093
01:16:24,831 --> 01:16:27,584
For now, they're contained on their planet.

1094
01:16:27,667 --> 01:16:28,960
Time is not on our side.

1095
01:16:29,419 --> 01:16:30,420
Where are they?

1096
01:16:31,254 --> 01:16:32,672
High surface temperatures limit

1097
01:16:32,714 --> 01:16:36,009
their above-ground activity
to just a few hours a day.

1098
01:16:37,344 --> 01:16:39,763
What's most alarming is the rate

1099
01:16:39,846 --> 01:16:42,224
at which their military power is expanding.

1100
01:17:03,745 --> 01:17:05,664
But they have not yet moved against us.

1101
01:17:05,789 --> 01:17:06,790
No.

1102
01:17:10,210 --> 01:17:12,337
They're planning to colonize another planet

1103
01:17:12,379 --> 01:17:14,089
before they breed themselves
into extinction.

1104
01:17:14,172 --> 01:17:15,465
Our orders are to defeat them

1105
01:17:15,549 --> 01:17:17,884
before they pose an irreversible threat.

1106
01:17:17,926 --> 01:17:20,220
Their very existence is a threat.

1107
01:17:20,303 --> 01:17:21,596
Is that clear, Commander?

1108
01:17:23,431 --> 01:17:25,600
- Clear, sir.
- Good.

1109
01:17:26,101 --> 01:17:27,894
Carry on, Colonel.

1110
01:17:30,188 --> 01:17:32,357
We will begin with photo real simulations

1111
01:17:32,399 --> 01:17:34,818
to best approximate real battles.

1112
01:17:35,026 --> 01:17:37,529
You will command overall strategy.

1113
01:17:37,571 --> 01:17:40,615
Your toon leaders will
each command a battle group.

1114
01:17:41,032 --> 01:17:43,076
You will issue orders to them.

1115
01:17:43,910 --> 01:17:46,204
They will issue orders
to their squadrons of drone pilots.

1116
01:18:21,114 --> 01:18:22,115
Finally,

1117
01:18:22,157 --> 01:18:24,242
your entire fleet must support

1118
01:18:24,284 --> 01:18:27,287
and protect your most important asset.

1119
01:18:28,663 --> 01:18:32,125
$70 billion of pure destruction.

1120
01:18:32,751 --> 01:18:34,961
The MD. 500.

1121
01:18:35,086 --> 01:18:37,422
Which Petra is trained to fire.

1122
01:18:37,756 --> 01:18:38,757
M.D.?

1123
01:18:38,798 --> 01:18:40,717
Molecular Detachment Device.

1124
01:18:41,134 --> 01:18:42,802
We call her "the little Doctor."

1125
01:18:44,179 --> 01:18:46,932
Particle beams accelerate
from her twin barrels.

1126
01:18:46,973 --> 01:18:49,601
At the focus point, they reach
critical effective mass.

1127
01:18:49,809 --> 01:18:51,353
A chain reaction spreads outwards,

1128
01:18:51,436 --> 01:18:53,146
shattering molecular bonds.

1129
01:18:53,188 --> 01:18:54,648
Leaves nothing standing.

1130
01:18:54,814 --> 01:18:56,775
That's the beauty of the little Doctor.

1131
01:18:56,816 --> 01:18:59,819
No need to identify
a specific ship for the queen.

1132
01:18:59,861 --> 01:19:02,989
The chain reaction
takes out an entire swarm.

1133
01:19:04,032 --> 01:19:06,326
But I'll only get one shot.

1134
01:19:06,785 --> 01:19:08,203
Once the Formics see how she works,

1135
01:19:08,286 --> 01:19:09,913
they won't clump together again.

1136
01:19:12,207 --> 01:19:15,335
You will have to win this war
one battle at a time.

1137
01:19:16,294 --> 01:19:17,712
Once our battle fleet is detected

1138
01:19:17,837 --> 01:19:20,173
entering the Formic solar system,

1139
01:19:20,257 --> 01:19:22,842
we will have no alternative but to engage.

1140
01:19:22,968 --> 01:19:25,428
I trust we have chosen our commander well.

1141
01:19:25,512 --> 01:19:26,930
There's greatness in him, sir.

1142
01:19:27,013 --> 01:19:28,348
And a killer instinct too, I hope.

1143
01:19:28,890 --> 01:19:30,684
Absolutely.

1144
01:19:31,226 --> 01:19:33,353
Let's hope he's all you claim him to be.

1145
01:19:33,812 --> 01:19:35,522
We'll be with you soon.

1146
01:19:36,064 --> 01:19:37,232
Goodnight.

1147
01:19:37,857 --> 01:19:39,192
Goodnight, sir.

1148
01:19:40,527 --> 01:19:43,405
"Dear Valentine...
So this is Command School.

1149
01:19:43,488 --> 01:19:44,781
"I'm finally here.

1150
01:19:44,864 --> 01:19:47,617
"Being a third, I've always
been so afraid I might fail.

1151
01:19:47,701 --> 01:19:48,868
"That I might not measure up.

1152
01:19:49,536 --> 01:19:51,413
"But they made me a leader.

1153
01:19:51,496 --> 01:19:52,539
"And I promise you

1154
01:19:52,580 --> 01:19:54,833
"that I'll do everything
I can to win this war.

1155
01:19:54,874 --> 01:19:57,002
"I know if anything ever happened to you,

1156
01:19:57,043 --> 01:19:58,503
"I would never forgive myself."

1157
01:19:58,545 --> 01:19:59,587
What are they doing?

1158
01:19:59,838 --> 01:20:01,506
Harvesting water.

1159
01:20:01,715 --> 01:20:03,550
If you're going to use me,
I need to be closer.

1160
01:20:04,092 --> 01:20:05,385
Too risky. Let's not reveal our best weapon

1161
01:20:05,510 --> 01:20:07,178
in what should be an easy attack.

1162
01:20:07,220 --> 01:20:09,514
Alai, Bean, your Dreads peel away.

1163
01:20:09,556 --> 01:20:12,309
Track them from below the ice
and mirror their path.

1164
01:20:18,064 --> 01:20:19,733
They're swarming!

1165
01:20:19,774 --> 01:20:21,359
- They see us!
- Deploy all drones!

1166
01:20:21,401 --> 01:20:23,194
Give me four hyperbolic formations

1167
01:20:23,236 --> 01:20:25,113
with 90 degree offsets!

1168
01:20:33,538 --> 01:20:34,914
Open fire!

1169
01:20:35,081 --> 01:20:37,876
Bean, Alai, on my call,
fire directly up into the ice!

1170
01:20:37,917 --> 01:20:39,085
We're gonna shred 'em!

1171
01:20:45,091 --> 01:20:47,344
- In three, two, one...
- All right!

1172
01:20:47,427 --> 01:20:48,762
Now!

1173
01:21:07,113 --> 01:21:08,490
"As our training progresses,

1174
01:21:08,615 --> 01:21:09,991
"the simulations are becoming

1175
01:21:10,075 --> 01:21:12,035
"more and more complex, and real.

1176
01:21:12,118 --> 01:21:14,162
"The pressure to win, day after day,

1177
01:21:14,245 --> 01:21:15,955
"month after month, is intense.

1178
01:21:15,997 --> 01:21:17,457
"We get very little sleep.

1179
01:21:17,540 --> 01:21:19,125
"Some days, it's hard to keep up."

1180
01:21:19,417 --> 01:21:21,127
- I got the breakaway!
- Great work, Bean!

1181
01:21:21,169 --> 01:21:23,129
Squadrons 43 through 57,

1182
01:21:23,171 --> 01:21:25,632
split to quadrant Foxtrot, 38, 89!

1183
01:21:25,715 --> 01:21:27,801
Ender, watch our right flank!
We need backup for Bernard.

1184
01:21:27,842 --> 01:21:28,968
I see it! Bernard, you flank them!

1185
01:21:29,010 --> 01:21:31,054
Copy that. Using 10 through 18!

1186
01:21:31,179 --> 01:21:32,931
Alai, peel right!

1187
01:21:32,972 --> 01:21:35,308
Dink, compensate for the pull of planet G8

1188
01:21:35,350 --> 01:21:36,518
and go full throttle!

1189
01:21:36,601 --> 01:21:38,269
Bean, mop up in sector Sierra!

1190
01:21:38,311 --> 01:21:40,105
I got a sprinter left in Lima!

1191
01:21:40,146 --> 01:21:41,523
Do Sierra now!

1192
01:21:41,648 --> 01:21:43,525
Bernard, watch your speed!

1193
01:21:43,608 --> 01:21:45,819
Dink, you are closing too fast!

1194
01:21:45,944 --> 01:21:48,113
- You said full throttle!
- Pull back now, Dink!

1195
01:22:12,429 --> 01:22:13,930
We can't absorb these kind of losses!

1196
01:22:14,013 --> 01:22:16,057
War isn't a game where you get
to reboot and start over!

1197
01:22:16,224 --> 01:22:18,393
Sir, I can't win if I don't take any risks.

1198
01:22:18,685 --> 01:22:20,520
Nobody's saying not to take risks.

1199
01:22:20,562 --> 01:22:22,397
Just don't try and control everything.

1200
01:22:22,480 --> 01:22:24,524
Let Bean improvise in the mop-ups.

1201
01:22:24,566 --> 01:22:26,025
You focus on the big picture.

1202
01:22:26,109 --> 01:22:29,446
- Delegate more to your teams!
- My teams are burned out!

1203
01:22:29,696 --> 01:22:32,031
How can they be effective
if they don't get any sleep?

1204
01:22:32,157 --> 01:22:33,825
Sleep deprivation is part of your training!

1205
01:22:33,867 --> 01:22:35,493
A battle with the Formics
could last for days!

1206
01:22:35,702 --> 01:22:36,828
If I'd been smarter,

1207
01:22:36,870 --> 01:22:38,580
I could have annihilated
Petra's little Doctor

1208
01:22:38,663 --> 01:22:39,998
while you were micro-managing Bean!

1209
01:22:40,039 --> 01:22:41,583
That can't happen, understand?

1210
01:22:43,042 --> 01:22:45,044
- Yes, sir.
- Do you?

1211
01:22:45,795 --> 01:22:47,380
'Cause I've trained others.

1212
01:22:47,714 --> 01:22:49,215
Each one so hopeful.

1213
01:22:50,049 --> 01:22:51,593
Each one ultimately a failure.

1214
01:22:53,761 --> 01:22:56,848
All right, Colonel. He understands.

1215
01:23:03,188 --> 01:23:04,689
So I'm not the first?

1216
01:23:04,731 --> 01:23:05,940
No.

1217
01:23:06,232 --> 01:23:07,901
But you will be the last.

1218
01:23:10,111 --> 01:23:12,280
There's no time to train anyone else.

1219
01:23:14,407 --> 01:23:16,367
Son, tomorrow Colonel Raokham will run

1220
01:23:16,409 --> 01:23:17,911
your final simulation.

1221
01:23:19,412 --> 01:23:22,248
And if I win tomorrow? What happens?

1222
01:23:22,332 --> 01:23:25,251
You will be ready to face the real enemy.

1223
01:23:29,088 --> 01:23:31,633
And you will be the finest
commander we've ever trained.

1224
01:23:39,933 --> 01:23:42,810
One more simulation
and I may have to go to war.

1225
01:23:42,936 --> 01:23:44,979
What happens when it's no longer a game?

1226
01:23:45,063 --> 01:23:46,105
Real war is different.

1227
01:23:46,314 --> 01:23:48,608
I still know nothing about my enemy.

1228
01:23:48,775 --> 01:23:50,610
What if they could talk to us?

1229
01:23:50,652 --> 01:23:51,778
They can't.

1230
01:23:51,819 --> 01:23:53,321
Dissections show no vocal chords.

1231
01:23:53,488 --> 01:23:55,573
There are other ways to communicate.

1232
01:23:58,952 --> 01:24:00,078
Ender, this is not a conversation

1233
01:24:00,119 --> 01:24:01,454
we should be having at 1:00 a.m.

1234
01:24:01,538 --> 01:24:04,123
What if they could "think" to one another?

1235
01:24:08,586 --> 01:24:09,963
What if we could "think" to them?

1236
01:24:10,505 --> 01:24:12,006
We need to sleep.

1237
01:24:12,090 --> 01:24:13,925
We have a graduation battle tomorrow.

1238
01:24:16,469 --> 01:24:17,637
Right.

1239
01:24:19,138 --> 01:24:20,348
We're gonna get crushed.

1240
01:24:20,640 --> 01:24:22,684
We won't be crushed. We have you.

1241
01:24:22,976 --> 01:24:24,686
Now go to sleep.

1242
01:24:24,769 --> 01:24:26,104
Goodnight, Petra.

1243
01:24:26,187 --> 01:24:27,438
Goodnight, Ender.

1244
01:24:32,485 --> 01:24:34,195
You still think he's "the one"?

1245
01:24:34,821 --> 01:24:36,114
We're committed.

1246
01:24:37,699 --> 01:24:40,410
This boy has the empathy
to think like a Formic.

1247
01:24:43,037 --> 01:24:45,999
To understand them, anticipate them.

1248
01:24:52,505 --> 01:24:53,881
He's not ready.

1249
01:24:56,342 --> 01:24:57,885
You're never "ready."

1250
01:25:01,139 --> 01:25:03,516
You go when you're "ready enough."

1251
01:25:11,316 --> 01:25:12,317
Easy, sir.

1252
01:25:13,067 --> 01:25:14,319
It's graduation day.

1253
01:25:25,204 --> 01:25:26,205
Good luck, sir.

1254
01:25:33,755 --> 01:25:35,089
Attention!

1255
01:25:38,718 --> 01:25:39,719
At ease.

1256
01:25:41,012 --> 01:25:42,263
Sir...

1257
01:25:42,388 --> 01:25:43,389
We have an audience.

1258
01:25:46,059 --> 01:25:47,518
Commander Wiggin,

1259
01:25:48,269 --> 01:25:51,564
the Strategos is here today
to witness your final simulation.

1260
01:25:52,398 --> 01:25:53,858
If you are successful,

1261
01:25:53,900 --> 01:25:55,735
he will endorse your promotion

1262
01:25:55,777 --> 01:25:59,364
to Battle Commander of the entire fleet.

1263
01:25:59,405 --> 01:26:00,448
Yes, sir!

1264
01:26:00,573 --> 01:26:03,326
This simulation is staged
around the enemy's home planet.

1265
01:26:03,534 --> 01:26:05,244
Good luck, Commander.

1266
01:26:05,745 --> 01:26:06,871
Thank you, sir.

1267
01:26:12,293 --> 01:26:13,920
Stay calm.

1268
01:26:14,295 --> 01:26:15,296
Shoot straight.

1269
01:26:17,757 --> 01:26:19,050
Here we go.

1270
01:26:57,505 --> 01:26:58,756
They're waiting.

1271
01:26:58,840 --> 01:27:00,925
Maybe they think we come in peace.

1272
01:27:01,134 --> 01:27:02,719
I don't think Mazer intends for us

1273
01:27:02,802 --> 01:27:04,429
to find a diplomatic solution.

1274
01:27:10,101 --> 01:27:11,853
What's he waiting for?

1275
01:27:13,146 --> 01:27:14,981
Just give him a minute.

1276
01:27:17,442 --> 01:27:18,818
Ender, what do we do?

1277
01:27:22,989 --> 01:27:24,157
Ender...

1278
01:27:24,449 --> 01:27:26,659
The enemy's gate is down.

1279
01:27:49,474 --> 01:27:50,516
Petra. You're up.

1280
01:27:50,558 --> 01:27:52,643
They're spread too wide
for a chain reaction.

1281
01:27:52,685 --> 01:27:53,686
She's right.

1282
01:27:53,770 --> 01:27:55,521
Just let him follow his instincts.

1283
01:27:55,563 --> 01:27:56,898
All battle groups deploy drones.

1284
01:27:57,023 --> 01:27:58,399
Protect your carriers.

1285
01:27:58,483 --> 01:28:00,860
Alai! You're squadron five! Engage!

1286
01:28:13,372 --> 01:28:14,749
This is suicide.

1287
01:28:31,057 --> 01:28:32,058
Oh, crap...

1288
01:28:32,433 --> 01:28:33,601
They're swarming.

1289
01:28:36,562 --> 01:28:38,064
Clumped enough for you now, Petra?

1290
01:28:38,105 --> 01:28:39,941
Once I fire, I need time to recharge.

1291
01:28:40,900 --> 01:28:42,068
Understood.

1292
01:28:42,109 --> 01:28:43,277
Just go for the center.

1293
01:28:45,738 --> 01:28:46,739
Fire now!

1294
01:29:11,597 --> 01:29:12,765
She did it.

1295
01:29:13,432 --> 01:29:14,725
Yeah.

1296
01:29:22,733 --> 01:29:23,943
Give me false color.

1297
01:29:33,286 --> 01:29:34,287
We're not done yet.

1298
01:29:34,537 --> 01:29:36,956
- But we are so screwed...
- No, we're not.

1299
01:29:37,039 --> 01:29:39,250
- Charged, Petra?
- No. I need two minutes.

1300
01:29:39,292 --> 01:29:41,294
All fighters fall back
and surround Petra's ship!

1301
01:29:41,460 --> 01:29:42,795
Copy that.

1302
01:29:42,837 --> 01:29:44,130
I want rings within rings.

1303
01:29:44,255 --> 01:29:46,632
Layers upon layer. Every fighter we have!

1304
01:29:52,805 --> 01:29:55,016
Ender, you're gonna leave
our transporters defenseless!

1305
01:29:55,099 --> 01:29:56,309
If we're gonna win this battle, Dink,

1306
01:29:56,392 --> 01:29:57,476
it's all or nothing now!

1307
01:29:57,810 --> 01:29:59,020
When the outer layer is hit,

1308
01:29:59,103 --> 01:30:00,980
the wreckage will continue to
drift with us, like a shield.

1309
01:30:01,063 --> 01:30:02,064
Do it now!

1310
01:30:02,231 --> 01:30:04,400
He's abandoning his entire fleet.

1311
01:30:04,525 --> 01:30:07,236
He's in command.
There's no stopping him now.

1312
01:30:07,862 --> 01:30:09,822
Ninety seconds, Ender!

1313
01:30:19,999 --> 01:30:21,000
No, no... No!

1314
01:30:22,001 --> 01:30:23,252
I'm losing my carriers!

1315
01:30:24,587 --> 01:30:25,630
My Dreadnaughts are out!

1316
01:30:25,671 --> 01:30:27,673
I don't care about Dreadnaughts!

1317
01:30:27,757 --> 01:30:29,008
Just protect Petra!

1318
01:30:29,091 --> 01:30:31,093
Like we protected Alai
when we fought Bonzo!

1319
01:30:31,177 --> 01:30:32,386
I hope you know what you're doing.

1320
01:30:32,470 --> 01:30:34,138
- Ready, Petra?
- In 60 seconds!

1321
01:30:34,180 --> 01:30:35,514
What am I aiming for?

1322
01:30:39,185 --> 01:30:40,519
The planet.

1323
01:30:41,187 --> 01:30:42,188
What?

1324
01:30:42,229 --> 01:30:45,107
If we destroy the planet,
we destroy the queens.

1325
01:30:46,359 --> 01:30:47,526
Game over.

1326
01:30:47,568 --> 01:30:49,695
Ender, my targeting sensor
needs a clear line of sight!

1327
01:30:50,029 --> 01:30:51,656
We will clear a path!

1328
01:30:51,697 --> 01:30:54,033
All fighters maintain a clockwise rotation!

1329
01:30:54,075 --> 01:30:55,701
Focus all firepower forward!

1330
01:31:06,837 --> 01:31:08,506
Ender, we're entering their atmosphere!

1331
01:31:08,673 --> 01:31:09,840
We need to slow down!

1332
01:31:09,882 --> 01:31:11,384
We can't! We're one unit now.

1333
01:31:11,467 --> 01:31:12,468
We're not equipped to handle

1334
01:31:12,551 --> 01:31:13,844
the heat of passage through an atmosphere!

1335
01:31:13,886 --> 01:31:15,179
Our drones are our heat shield.

1336
01:31:15,221 --> 01:31:16,222
Keep falling.

1337
01:31:16,305 --> 01:31:17,807
Let gravity do the work.

1338
01:31:30,027 --> 01:31:31,904
The shield won't hold forever!

1339
01:31:31,988 --> 01:31:33,739
We don't need forever.

1340
01:31:34,615 --> 01:31:36,242
Thirty seconds!

1341
01:31:36,450 --> 01:31:37,743
I still don't have a clear shot.

1342
01:31:37,827 --> 01:31:39,662
- We're burning up!
- Bean, on my count,

1343
01:31:39,745 --> 01:31:42,039
accelerate your fighters
from the nose of the formation

1344
01:31:42,081 --> 01:31:43,916
- in a continuous stream.
- Yes, sir!

1345
01:31:44,000 --> 01:31:45,209
Like bullets from a rifle,

1346
01:31:45,251 --> 01:31:46,544
you will clear a visual for Petra!

1347
01:31:48,087 --> 01:31:49,922
We will drill a hole through this swarm!

1348
01:31:50,006 --> 01:31:51,090
Petra, you will only get a second.

1349
01:31:51,132 --> 01:31:52,133
That's all I need!

1350
01:31:52,633 --> 01:31:55,302
In three, two, one... Now, Bean!

1351
01:32:15,781 --> 01:32:18,034
Shield integrity's at 5%!

1352
01:32:20,619 --> 01:32:22,079
- Now, Petra! Now!
- Seven seconds!

1353
01:32:22,121 --> 01:32:23,497
They've broken the shield!

1354
01:32:26,000 --> 01:32:27,793
Fire, Petra! We're out of time!

1355
01:33:12,880 --> 01:33:15,299
- We did it! Yeah!
- Yes!

1356
01:33:17,301 --> 01:33:19,845
- Great job, Ender!
- Yes! Thank you!

1357
01:33:20,179 --> 01:33:21,722
Good game, Ender!

1358
01:33:21,806 --> 01:33:22,807
Good job, guys!

1359
01:33:22,848 --> 01:33:23,849
Yeah!

1360
01:33:26,185 --> 01:33:27,645
How about that?

1361
01:33:31,398 --> 01:33:32,483
Game over.

1362
01:33:41,867 --> 01:33:42,868
What's he saying?

1363
01:33:45,746 --> 01:33:47,540
Restoring Ansible connection.

1364
01:34:24,994 --> 01:34:26,120
What is this?

1365
01:34:27,913 --> 01:34:29,748
Why are we watching these images?

1366
01:34:39,300 --> 01:34:40,843
Ender...

1367
01:34:42,261 --> 01:34:43,387
Thank you.

1368
01:34:44,597 --> 01:34:47,683
Brilliant. Absolutely brilliant.

1369
01:34:48,017 --> 01:34:49,768
Thank God for you, son.

1370
01:34:49,852 --> 01:34:52,021
Why are these images in the program?

1371
01:34:52,688 --> 01:34:53,898
Ender...

1372
01:34:54,773 --> 01:34:55,900
We won.

1373
01:34:58,152 --> 01:34:59,612
What do you mean, "we won"?

1374
01:35:01,572 --> 01:35:03,324
I beat him.

1375
01:35:03,949 --> 01:35:05,868
He runs the simulations.

1376
01:35:06,202 --> 01:35:07,620
He said it was a game!

1377
01:35:07,703 --> 01:35:09,288
It was them or us, Ender.

1378
01:35:09,455 --> 01:35:11,040
There was no other way.

1379
01:35:12,625 --> 01:35:14,168
With this victory,

1380
01:35:14,960 --> 01:35:17,296
you've won all future battles.

1381
01:35:17,838 --> 01:35:19,715
You destroyed them.

1382
01:35:20,132 --> 01:35:21,884
For all of us.

1383
01:35:46,158 --> 01:35:47,576
Stand down.

1384
01:35:47,660 --> 01:35:48,827
Move, move, please!

1385
01:35:48,869 --> 01:35:50,204
- Move!
- Make a way.

1386
01:35:54,833 --> 01:35:57,169
- Ender...
- Stay away from me!

1387
01:35:58,003 --> 01:35:59,546
- You lied!
- Son, we were afraid

1388
01:35:59,630 --> 01:36:00,923
- if we told you, you might...
- What?

1389
01:36:01,006 --> 01:36:02,508
Refuse to play?

1390
01:36:02,591 --> 01:36:05,427
I've killed an entire species!

1391
01:36:05,511 --> 01:36:07,346
They would have done the same to us.

1392
01:36:07,429 --> 01:36:10,015
No! They waited.
What were they waiting for?

1393
01:36:10,099 --> 01:36:12,101
Who cares?

1394
01:36:12,184 --> 01:36:13,769
We lost 1,000 men

1395
01:36:13,852 --> 01:36:15,229
on the transporters you abandoned!

1396
01:36:15,312 --> 01:36:17,523
I abandoned them in order to win!

1397
01:36:17,564 --> 01:36:20,609
Yes! And they died proudly! For us!

1398
01:36:20,693 --> 01:36:22,528
They might not have died at all!

1399
01:36:28,575 --> 01:36:30,035
If I'd known it was real,

1400
01:36:30,077 --> 01:36:31,537
- I would have...
- What?

1401
01:36:31,620 --> 01:36:33,747
Called for "a dialogue"?
They can't even speak.

1402
01:36:33,831 --> 01:36:36,458
Watched them! What were they thinking?

1403
01:36:36,542 --> 01:36:38,961
Were they building an army
for a second invasion?

1404
01:36:39,044 --> 01:36:41,046
Or... Or simply preparing
to defend themselves...

1405
01:36:41,088 --> 01:36:42,172
Ender, stop...

1406
01:36:42,214 --> 01:36:43,632
...from us?

1407
01:36:44,258 --> 01:36:47,136
They came to Earth to establish a colony.

1408
01:36:47,219 --> 01:36:48,387
We chased them away.

1409
01:36:48,470 --> 01:36:50,639
And in 50 years, they never returned.

1410
01:36:50,723 --> 01:36:52,016
Makes no difference now.

1411
01:36:52,057 --> 01:36:54,643
I will bear the shame
of this genocide forever.

1412
01:36:54,727 --> 01:36:58,230
No. You will be remembered as a hero!

1413
01:36:58,314 --> 01:37:00,482
I will be remembered as a killer!

1414
01:37:01,567 --> 01:37:02,735
It was us or them.

1415
01:37:02,776 --> 01:37:04,528
And you're sure we've killed
every last one of them?

1416
01:37:04,570 --> 01:37:06,322
I saw their whole planet destroyed.

1417
01:37:06,405 --> 01:37:07,823
How do you know
if there was another colony?

1418
01:37:07,906 --> 01:37:09,325
- Or another queen out there?
- There isn't!

1419
01:37:09,408 --> 01:37:11,493
We won!

1420
01:37:12,077 --> 01:37:14,079
- That's all that matters.
- No.

1421
01:37:16,123 --> 01:37:19,084
The way we win matters.

1422
01:37:27,009 --> 01:37:28,552
Don't hurt him.

1423
01:37:51,992 --> 01:37:53,911
Go on. We need to let him rest.

1424
01:37:53,952 --> 01:37:55,579
May I stay with him?

1425
01:37:57,664 --> 01:37:59,166
Just so he's not alone.

1426
01:38:00,626 --> 01:38:01,627
Please?

1427
01:38:02,961 --> 01:38:05,047
Yes, of course.

1428
01:38:18,310 --> 01:38:20,479
Come on. Just let him rest.

1429
01:38:38,330 --> 01:38:39,998
What if they could talk to us?

1430
01:38:45,337 --> 01:38:46,755
What were they thinking?

1431
01:38:53,053 --> 01:38:54,221
Valentine!

1432
01:38:59,685 --> 01:39:01,186
What if we could "think" to them?

1433
01:39:06,191 --> 01:39:07,359
Valentine!

1434
01:39:07,401 --> 01:39:08,652
Ended

1435
01:39:09,528 --> 01:39:10,612
Ender, wait!

1436
01:39:11,947 --> 01:39:13,282
Ended

1437
01:39:14,867 --> 01:39:16,869
What are you doing, Ender?

1438
01:39:16,910 --> 01:39:19,288
- I know what she wants!
- Ended

1439
01:39:19,872 --> 01:39:20,873
Warning,

1440
01:39:20,956 --> 01:39:23,208
you are leaving an
oxygen-balanced environment.

1441
01:39:23,250 --> 01:39:24,751
Ender, stop!

1442
01:39:26,211 --> 01:39:27,212
It's not safe!

1443
01:39:28,213 --> 01:39:29,465
Ended

1444
01:39:36,722 --> 01:39:38,599
Breathe. Just breathe.

1445
01:39:49,401 --> 01:39:52,196
In the mind game, I saw this place.

1446
01:39:53,739 --> 01:39:54,990
What are you talking about?

1447
01:39:55,407 --> 01:39:58,243
The Formics accessed the game through me.

1448
01:39:58,785 --> 01:40:01,747
Their thoughts. My dreams.
All mixed together.

1449
01:40:06,043 --> 01:40:07,503
They were trying to communicate.

1450
01:40:09,630 --> 01:40:10,756
What are you doing?

1451
01:40:14,009 --> 01:40:15,260
Go back.

1452
01:40:16,261 --> 01:40:17,262
No.

1453
01:40:17,304 --> 01:40:18,305
Please...

1454
01:40:18,931 --> 01:40:20,265
I have to do this.

1455
01:40:54,466 --> 01:40:56,468
"Dear Valentine,

1456
01:40:56,552 --> 01:40:58,971
"I now know my dreams
were never my own.

1457
01:40:59,054 --> 01:41:00,764
"They came from her.

1458
01:41:01,723 --> 01:41:04,309
"She was always trying
to communicate with me.

1459
01:41:04,977 --> 01:41:08,146
"I know the Formics
better than any living soul.

1460
01:41:08,855 --> 01:41:10,732
"I stole their future from them.

1461
01:41:11,567 --> 01:41:13,735
"Now I must find a way to make amends."

1462
01:43:49,516 --> 01:43:51,309
You're dying.

1463
01:44:07,492 --> 01:44:09,077
Is it a queen?

1464
01:44:31,349 --> 01:44:33,393
I will find a new home.

1465
01:44:40,776 --> 01:44:42,194
I promise.

1466
01:44:57,250 --> 01:44:59,044
"I miss you, Valentine.

1467
01:44:59,878 --> 01:45:02,380
"You won't be hearing from me for a while.

1468
01:45:09,721 --> 01:45:13,433
"I need to find out
if I'm as gifted at peace as I am at war.

1469
01:45:15,143 --> 01:45:17,395
"They've awarded me the rank of Admiral

1470
01:45:17,437 --> 01:45:19,064
"and left me to my own devices.

1471
01:45:19,731 --> 01:45:21,399
"Which suits me fine.

1472
01:45:22,442 --> 01:45:23,819
"I'll travel the universe

1473
01:45:23,902 --> 01:45:26,196
"and carry with me a precious cargo.

1474
01:45:26,988 --> 01:45:28,907
"Because I have a promise to keep."

